1
00:01:31,221 --> 00:01:34,430
2008, SIRALA THAANDA,
ANDHRA-MAHARASHTRA BORDER, FOREST AREA

2
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,388
[chain rattling]

3
00:02:14,721 --> 00:02:15,388
Hey!

4
00:02:15,513 --> 00:02:16,805
Rajaiah! Srinaiah!

5
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,721
They are taking away the kids.
Come, guys.

6
00:02:43,055 --> 00:02:43,846
Dad!

7
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,430
Dad!

8
00:02:48,013 --> 00:02:49,471
- Damini!
- Dad!

9
00:02:49,596 --> 00:02:51,513
- Run away! Run away, dear!
- Dad!

10
00:02:51,846 --> 00:02:53,180
- Samba!
- Don't come near me!

11
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:57,971
Don't come, dear!

12
00:02:58,971 --> 00:03:00,013
Run away!

13
00:03:00,846 --> 00:03:01,680
Run away!

14
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,805
If you touch that girl,
it will jolt you.

15
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:22,596
I will see her end, leave me!

16
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:35,596
Brother,
they might come back at any moment.

17
00:03:35,721 --> 00:03:37,680
Yes, they will definitely come back.

18
00:03:37,805 --> 00:03:38,596
Hey!

19
00:03:38,805 --> 00:03:40,680
Sticks or anything else,
bring whatever you can find.

20
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,180
Let's see who will come back.

21
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:43,638
We won't spare anyone this time.

22
00:03:43,805 --> 00:03:47,430
If they ever dare to come here again,
fear should paralyze them.

23
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,763
Let's teach them a lesson.

24
00:03:48,888 --> 00:03:50,346
I lost Durga.

25
00:03:50,513 --> 00:03:54,013
I am not ready to lose my daughter.

26
00:03:55,471 --> 00:03:56,471
Damini!

27
00:04:10,596 --> 00:04:14,096
"O sparkling star of the drizzle!"

28
00:04:15,221 --> 00:04:18,596
"A precious pearl with a glowing smile!"

29
00:04:19,055 --> 00:04:21,055
'That moon
is just like you, dear.'

30
00:04:21,638 --> 00:04:23,930
'Nobody can touch it or hug it.'

31
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:29,138
'It gives courage to those
in darkness by giving them light.'

32
00:04:29,346 --> 00:04:33,888
"O This earth is beneath your legs."

33
00:04:34,096 --> 00:04:38,596
"It relishes bearing your weight"

34
00:04:38,763 --> 00:04:42,805
"O star that flashes like lightning..."

35
00:04:43,013 --> 00:04:47,513
"A warm welcome to you today."

36
00:04:48,596 --> 00:04:52,680
[vocals]

37
00:05:00,596 --> 00:05:01,471
CHANDLAPUR

38
00:05:01,596 --> 00:05:03,013
We've reached Chandlapur. Get down.

39
00:05:07,971 --> 00:05:08,971
- How are you doing?
- Come, dear.

40
00:05:09,138 --> 00:05:10,388
The whole village
is suffering from fatal fevers,

41
00:05:10,596 --> 00:05:12,096
but that village president
is doing nothing.

42
00:05:13,763 --> 00:05:15,805
While fatal fevers
are spreading across the village...

43
00:05:16,013 --> 00:05:18,471
you're the village president.
Aren't you supposed to stop this?

44
00:05:19,471 --> 00:05:20,888
Look at Venkat's daughter.

45
00:05:21,138 --> 00:05:23,180
There's not even
an RMP doctor in this village.

46
00:05:23,305 --> 00:05:24,763
Can this even be called a village?

47
00:05:26,138 --> 00:05:28,555
Brother Srisailam,
none of this is helping.

48
00:05:28,971 --> 00:05:30,390
You must resign.

49
00:05:30,471 --> 00:05:31,305
- What?
- Hey, man!

50
00:05:31,471 --> 00:05:34,721
- He must resign.
- [crowd]: He must!

51
00:05:34,971 --> 00:05:38,513
- He must resign.
- [crowd]: He must!

52
00:05:38,721 --> 00:05:41,138
After all that arguing, they've
finally come after my president's post!

53
00:05:41,263 --> 00:05:43,096
I'll talk to them.
You stay quiet. Hey!

54
00:05:43,263 --> 00:05:43,888
- He must resign.
- [crowd]: He must!

55
00:05:44,055 --> 00:05:44,721
Hey, stop it.

56
00:05:44,846 --> 00:05:45,888
- He must resign.
- [crowd]: He must!

57
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:47,596
Hey! Stop yelling
and listen to me.

58
00:05:48,055 --> 00:05:49,596
This coward...

59
00:05:50,055 --> 00:05:51,888
Don't call me a coward. I'm the president.
I'll lose my reputation.

60
00:05:52,013 --> 00:05:52,846
That's exactly what I'm saying.

61
00:05:52,971 --> 00:05:56,203
If I become the president
instead of him...

62
00:05:56,371 --> 00:05:58,496
Is that going to fix the problem?

63
00:05:58,638 --> 00:05:59,388
Tell me.

64
00:05:59,513 --> 00:06:00,430
It won't be solved, right?

65
00:06:00,555 --> 00:06:02,138
What is the use of making him resign?

66
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:03,555
What happened to the child?

67
00:06:04,638 --> 00:06:05,721
Lay her down over there.

68
00:06:08,805 --> 00:06:10,138
- Are you a doctor?
- Yes.

69
00:06:10,638 --> 00:06:11,638
Hold this.

70
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,013
Hey, she opened her eyes.

71
00:06:33,888 --> 00:06:35,221
- My child!
- Take her with you.

72
00:06:35,346 --> 00:06:36,388
Be careful.

73
00:06:37,055 --> 00:06:38,513
- - [both]:
- Thank you, sir.
- It's okay.

74
00:06:38,888 --> 00:06:39,930
Take care of her.

75
00:06:40,096 --> 00:06:41,680
She'll be conscious within an hour.

76
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:42,971
- Okay, sir.
- Bye, sir.

77
00:06:43,138 --> 00:06:46,221
You came like a god and saved that girl's
life... along with my president's post.

78
00:06:46,471 --> 00:06:47,680
Who are you?

79
00:06:48,346 --> 00:06:49,638
I am a herbal doctor.

80
00:06:49,846 --> 00:06:50,513
Is that so?

81
00:06:50,596 --> 00:06:53,221
I intend to start a small clinic
in the neighboring village.

82
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:55,596
Why go to the neighboring village?
Start the hospital in our village.

83
00:06:55,805 --> 00:06:57,388
You could save the lives of our people.

84
00:06:57,763 --> 00:06:59,305
What caused those injuries?

85
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:02,288
I fell in the forest when
I went to get herbs.

86
00:07:03,096 --> 00:07:05,388
I'm telling you this
from my jungle knowledge.

87
00:07:05,721 --> 00:07:08,721
You're the one saving people's lives, so
you should take good care of yourself too.

88
00:07:09,055 --> 00:07:11,513
That's not jungle knowledge.
It's general knowledge.

89
00:07:11,638 --> 00:07:12,346
Oopsh!

90
00:07:12,513 --> 00:07:13,471
Yes, I meant the same thing.

91
00:07:13,638 --> 00:07:15,638
- General knowledge.
- What's your name, girl?

92
00:07:15,888 --> 00:07:16,930
Damini.

93
00:07:17,013 --> 00:07:18,971
- Oh, the way she said it was so sweet.
- Take them.

94
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:19,680
Come, sir.

95
00:07:19,805 --> 00:07:20,888
- Let's go, dear.
- Go on.

96
00:07:23,221 --> 00:07:25,471
People need
to have some patience.

97
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,763
How can you demand
my resignation for every little issue?

98
00:07:27,846 --> 00:07:28,555
Exactly.

99
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,805
We have a doctor now.

100
00:07:30,096 --> 00:07:31,638
Our problem is solved now, isn't it?

101
00:07:31,846 --> 00:07:32,638
- Yes!
- That's it.

102
00:07:32,846 --> 00:07:33,596
Alright, let's head home.

103
00:07:33,805 --> 00:07:36,346
- Brother Srisailam!
- [crowd]: Long live!

104
00:07:38,596 --> 00:07:39,096
[children mocking]

105
00:07:39,305 --> 00:07:40,555
Why can't you speak for once?

106
00:07:48,805 --> 00:07:49,805
Just speak for a moment.

107
00:07:49,971 --> 00:07:51,471
[children mocking]

108
00:07:57,346 --> 00:07:59,388
Can't you speak?

109
00:08:02,305 --> 00:08:03,846
What happened to him?

110
00:08:07,305 --> 00:08:09,096
- Damini's touch is electrocuting us.
- Let's go, run!

111
00:08:09,305 --> 00:08:10,555
Run, run...

112
00:08:11,596 --> 00:08:12,638
Friends?

113
00:08:14,805 --> 00:08:15,846
Oopsh!

114
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:27,430
PRINCIPAL.
- You're scaring the kids.

115
00:08:27,555 --> 00:08:28,680
Don't act innocent.

116
00:08:29,305 --> 00:08:32,346
After causing all this trouble,
what's the point of crying now?

117
00:08:34,971 --> 00:08:38,138
The other day, you gave
electric shocks to all the students.

118
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:41,180
Since then,
admissions to our school have dropped.

119
00:08:42,263 --> 00:08:44,013
Tell me your father's phone number.

120
00:08:46,555 --> 00:08:47,555
Sir, please, sir.

121
00:08:47,805 --> 00:08:49,013
Please, sir... please!

122
00:08:49,221 --> 00:08:51,263
Sir... please! Please, sir!

123
00:08:51,388 --> 00:08:55,263
[screaming]

124
00:08:57,888 --> 00:09:00,138
<i>There isn't any hospital
which I haven't visited,</i>

125
00:09:00,471 --> 00:09:01,930
<i>or a doctor I haven't consulted so far.</i>

126
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:04,055
<i>What has happened to my daughter, sir?</i>

127
00:09:04,263 --> 00:09:07,055
As per my observation
when she becomes emotional,

128
00:09:07,263 --> 00:09:08,680
her heart beat becomes abnormal,

129
00:09:09,013 --> 00:09:11,346
at that time when she touches anyone,

130
00:09:11,555 --> 00:09:14,430
<i>or anyone touches her will get a shock.</i>

131
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:22,221
<i>As per our medical records,
in the year 1970, in France,</i>

132
00:09:22,430 --> 00:09:25,263
<i>a case has been registered as
"Electric girl of Bornia".</i>

133
00:09:25,638 --> 00:09:28,138
<i>Whatever thing she touches
we could see sparks.</i>

134
00:09:28,430 --> 00:09:31,846
<i>Generally a human body
has a 0.5 volts of static current.</i>

135
00:09:32,263 --> 00:09:34,221
<i>It's a little more in
your daughter's case.</i>

136
00:09:34,471 --> 00:09:37,846
<i>As this is a peculiar case,
there is no cure for this.</i>

137
00:09:38,513 --> 00:09:40,180
<i>So, take care of your daughter.</i>

138
00:09:41,471 --> 00:09:44,346
[crowd chants in unison]

139
00:09:44,638 --> 00:09:45,555
Hail Lord Rama!

140
00:09:45,763 --> 00:09:47,888
[crowd continues chanting in unison]

141
00:09:48,513 --> 00:09:51,680
I did whatever I could as a father, lord.

142
00:09:52,263 --> 00:09:54,055
From this moment,
my child is in your hands.

143
00:09:54,305 --> 00:09:55,346
Hail Lord Rama.

144
00:10:00,471 --> 00:10:02,513
All the boys in the village
are afraid of her...

145
00:10:02,721 --> 00:10:03,930
But you became friends with her.

146
00:10:04,096 --> 00:10:06,805
If I see you with her again,
I'll deal with you myself.

147
00:10:07,430 --> 00:10:08,638
You're a mute child.

148
00:10:08,846 --> 00:10:10,096
- What if she gives you an electric shock?
- Malli!

149
00:10:10,305 --> 00:10:11,638
How could I know that?

150
00:10:12,055 --> 00:10:13,055
Don't go with her again.

151
00:10:13,263 --> 00:10:14,430
Shh...

152
00:10:18,346 --> 00:10:19,221
Hey, you!

153
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:20,763
You're still going with her
even after I warned you!

154
00:10:20,971 --> 00:10:22,138
Hey, oldie, shut up.

155
00:10:22,346 --> 00:10:23,555
Who's the oldie here?

156
00:10:24,055 --> 00:10:25,846
I'm only twenty years older than you,
and you call me old?

157
00:10:26,055 --> 00:10:26,888
- Oops!
- Hey.

158
00:10:28,346 --> 00:10:29,096
Malli.

159
00:10:29,596 --> 00:10:30,555
Oh, Malli.

160
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:33,846
Do you know who the real
lucky ones are, children?

161
00:10:33,971 --> 00:10:35,680
The one who owns
a bat and ball, Grandpa.

162
00:10:37,221 --> 00:10:39,305
The one who has a big house
like the village president.

163
00:10:41,471 --> 00:10:43,138
Not the ones who own big houses.

164
00:10:43,555 --> 00:10:47,763
The truly lucky ones are those
who live happily in a joint family.

165
00:10:48,513 --> 00:10:49,930
What do you mean, grandfather?

166
00:10:49,955 --> 00:10:55,955
A family where grandparents, parents,
uncles, and aunties all stay together.

167
00:10:56,129 --> 00:10:59,046
If everyone lives together,
that's true happiness.

168
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:03,721
If God has taken something from us...

169
00:11:03,930 --> 00:11:06,680
...it only means
He has something better planned for us.

170
00:11:16,096 --> 00:11:17,596
I suddenly thought of my mother.

171
00:11:17,888 --> 00:11:20,471
That's why we shouldn't feel sad.

172
00:11:20,496 --> 00:11:22,787
We should stay happy
as much as possible.

173
00:11:25,221 --> 00:11:27,555
[indistinct chatter]

174
00:11:32,013 --> 00:11:33,430
<i>Malli!</i>

175
00:11:38,346 --> 00:11:40,805
BHOOMPALLY VILLAGE

176
00:11:41,805 --> 00:11:42,846
[slurping marrow loudly]

177
00:11:44,430 --> 00:11:45,430
[slurps loudly]

178
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:48,971
[slurps more loudly]

179
00:11:49,221 --> 00:11:50,721
[slurping continues louder]

180
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:51,388
[loud slurp]

181
00:11:51,596 --> 00:11:52,388
Stop!

182
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:55,638
We planned to send offering
to the temple tomorrow, right?

183
00:11:56,221 --> 00:11:57,680
Tamarind rice or curd rice?

184
00:11:58,096 --> 00:11:58,763
Tamarind rice.

185
00:11:58,971 --> 00:12:00,638
- Curd rice.
- Tamarind rice.

186
00:12:00,846 --> 00:12:02,471
- Curd rice.
- Tamarind rice.

187
00:12:03,755 --> 00:12:05,546
- Curd rice!
- Tamarind rice!

188
00:12:06,555 --> 00:12:08,346
- Curd rice!
- Tamarind rice!

189
00:12:08,555 --> 00:12:09,888
What is this stubbornness?
It can't be your decision always.

190
00:12:10,096 --> 00:12:11,013
- Tamarind rice!
- Curd rice!

191
00:12:11,096 --> 00:12:12,888
Stop it! What is this nuisance?

192
00:12:15,055 --> 00:12:17,596
I spent years building this party and
handed it over to my eldest son to run...

193
00:12:17,846 --> 00:12:19,805
and now he switched to another party.

194
00:12:21,763 --> 00:12:22,888
Please take care of it very well.

195
00:12:23,096 --> 00:12:26,513
- Leadership of Balraju...
- [crowd]: May it flourish!

196
00:12:27,263 --> 00:12:30,263
That fellow grew up but not from mind.

197
00:12:30,788 --> 00:12:33,788
<i>Don't say that, do you think
everyone is like our younger son?</i>

198
00:12:33,888 --> 00:12:38,930
Hey, that fellow is roaming around
without getting married.

199
00:12:39,138 --> 00:12:41,763
- 1, 2, 3, 4...
- [in unison]: 1, 2, 3, 4...

200
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:45,096
My sons have become like this
but my grandsons are very good.

201
00:12:46,055 --> 00:12:49,138
Would an offspring learn differently?

202
00:12:49,346 --> 00:12:53,513
- I will sit in front seat...
- I will sit in front seat...

203
00:12:53,654 --> 00:12:55,071
Hey, stop it!

204
00:12:56,138 --> 00:12:58,388
Even you both are fighting
like you father's, huh?

205
00:13:00,013 --> 00:13:02,388
Your father's lost all the wealth
earned by my father.

206
00:13:02,721 --> 00:13:04,138
All the wasteful spending

207
00:13:05,096 --> 00:13:06,263
and debts have piled up on.

208
00:13:07,096 --> 00:13:09,763
They catch each others collars in the
morning but booze together at night.

209
00:13:11,013 --> 00:13:12,805
Hey, don't become like your fathers.

210
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:16,180
If this house is proper,

211
00:13:16,388 --> 00:13:18,388
that's because of my
elder daughter-in-law.

212
00:13:21,305 --> 00:13:22,513
- Padma...<i>-Yes?</i>

213
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,638
One more marrow bone.

214
00:13:24,263 --> 00:13:26,263
I served all the marrow bones
to you, father-in-law.

215
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:28,221
It's okay, dear.
I don't want. Let's it be.

216
00:13:30,104 --> 00:13:32,771
<i>Your daughter-in-law
won't serve you, come to me.</i>

217
00:13:32,896 --> 00:13:36,771
Hey, stupid!
I won't come, I won't.

218
00:13:41,930 --> 00:13:45,013
<i>What is this?
You came already, but you said you won't.</i>

219
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:08,971
Great man!

220
00:14:09,221 --> 00:14:12,055
If every village had someone
like him, everything would be fine.

221
00:14:12,162 --> 00:14:12,620
Yes.

222
00:14:12,930 --> 00:14:14,513
He is one among
us and one like us.

223
00:14:14,721 --> 00:14:16,138
PRAJADARANA PARTY.<i>Our beloved leader...</i>

224
00:14:16,471 --> 00:14:17,221
<i>Our youth leader...</i>

225
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:18,846
<i>Our Bhompalli's beloved son.</i>

226
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:21,563
<i>A grand welcome
to Brother Narala Yadagiri!</i>

227
00:14:21,821 --> 00:14:25,863
Our vote is to the symbol of Bulb!
Our vote is to the symbol of Bulb!

228
00:14:38,471 --> 00:14:40,555
As waves belong to the ocean...

229
00:14:40,805 --> 00:14:46,721
my deepest gratitude to my party cadre
who supported me and trusted my party,

230
00:14:46,971 --> 00:14:49,180
and to every one of my well-wishers.

231
00:14:53,971 --> 00:14:56,680
We are the ones who usually
remain in the opposition.

232
00:14:57,055 --> 00:15:00,138
In the next election,
this party's goal is to...

233
00:15:00,571 --> 00:15:04,362
bring us to power without
spending a single rupee.

234
00:15:05,805 --> 00:15:07,013
<i>What is that noise?</i>

235
00:15:07,221 --> 00:15:08,305
What's going on, Sapthagiri?

236
00:15:09,096 --> 00:15:09,930
What's the matter?

237
00:15:10,138 --> 00:15:11,013
PRAJADARANA PARTY.

238
00:15:11,930 --> 00:15:12,763
Brother!

239
00:15:13,346 --> 00:15:16,805
Seeing this buzz, it seems like
he's going to win this election.

240
00:15:17,805 --> 00:15:19,013
Is he our man or the opposition?

241
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:20,346
It's nothing like that, brother.

242
00:15:20,805 --> 00:15:21,138
You...

243
00:15:21,305 --> 00:15:21,971
Brother.

244
00:15:22,305 --> 00:15:27,680
He's the kind of person who
won't even buy a single cigarette.

245
00:15:28,388 --> 00:15:30,096
You don't know the real story.

246
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:31,346
Look there...

247
00:15:43,596 --> 00:15:44,555
He is a great man.

248
00:15:45,096 --> 00:15:49,388
My deepest gratitude to my party cadre
who supported me and trusted my party,

249
00:15:49,596 --> 00:15:51,388
and to every one of my well-wishers.

250
00:16:02,096 --> 00:16:03,180
Hey, Yadi!

251
00:16:03,596 --> 00:16:07,221
We have to admit it.
You gave yourself a great introduction.

252
00:16:08,846 --> 00:16:10,138
You should have blown
a whistle for him.

253
00:16:10,721 --> 00:16:13,638
Hey!
If you vote for the Sarpanch, it's proper.

254
00:16:13,846 --> 00:16:15,180
Why waste a vote on that chap?

255
00:16:17,596 --> 00:16:19,721
[people mocking]

256
00:16:40,229 --> 00:16:43,313
- Hey, what? You are coming on us...
- Oh no!

257
00:16:43,388 --> 00:16:44,763
Will you always keep fighting?

258
00:16:46,055 --> 00:16:48,180
Don't know whether you uphold your
grandfather's reputation or tarnish it...

259
00:16:56,471 --> 00:16:58,680
Your father, Mr. Naraala Nagabhushanam...

260
00:16:59,721 --> 00:17:02,346
wrote a will without your knowledge.

261
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:08,763
After 25 years, whichever of his
grandchildren has a child first...

262
00:17:09,388 --> 00:17:12,805
will inherit 80 acres
of property.

263
00:17:14,513 --> 00:17:16,055
- 80 acres? Where is it?
- Where is it?

264
00:17:16,721 --> 00:17:17,305
Wasn't all that gone long ago?

265
00:17:17,513 --> 00:17:18,805
If he wrote a will, he
should've written it in my name.

266
00:17:19,013 --> 00:17:20,263
Why did he write
it in his grandson's name?

267
00:17:21,721 --> 00:17:23,846
He knew you'd ruin the entire property.

268
00:17:24,846 --> 00:17:27,138
With the hope that he would be reborn...

269
00:17:28,305 --> 00:17:31,180
with the wish that he could
enjoy the entire property again.

270
00:17:31,513 --> 00:17:32,596
Perhaps he planned it this way.

271
00:17:33,096 --> 00:17:35,221
- Oh, my goodness!
- Alright, continue.

272
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:37,346
Even in death, the old man
left behind a massive headache.

273
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,846
- Sir, where is this 80 acre located?
- Lakshmi! Hey, Lakshmi!

274
00:17:44,388 --> 00:17:45,430
Where else would it be?

275
00:17:45,805 --> 00:17:46,846
It's tied up in court.

276
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,888
If you win, it'll be yours.

277
00:17:50,221 --> 00:17:52,388
Otherwise, it'll go
to the government.

278
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,221
Your wish.

279
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:55,805
Sir, sir, sir.

280
00:17:56,388 --> 00:17:57,388
Do I have any chance?

281
00:17:57,846 --> 00:17:59,055
Are you married?

282
00:17:59,305 --> 00:18:00,805
- No, sir.
- Then don't get married.

283
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,388
'Grandfather's property is mine.'

284
00:18:04,763 --> 00:18:05,971
'Let's see.'

285
00:18:14,263 --> 00:18:15,221
Get down!

286
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:19,721
- Mom, I brought my heir.
- Who is she?

287
00:18:19,930 --> 00:18:22,888
- Take her blessings.
- Bless me, mother-in-law!

288
00:18:23,096 --> 00:18:23,555
Who is she?

289
00:18:23,721 --> 00:18:25,596
Mummy, she is your daughter-in-law.

290
00:18:26,388 --> 00:18:27,555
He is your grandson...

291
00:18:27,888 --> 00:18:29,013
I'm going to become a father!

292
00:18:29,263 --> 00:18:31,013
Daughter-in-law? What
nonsense is this now?

293
00:18:31,763 --> 00:18:33,680
We need to be fast if
we need the property.

294
00:18:34,888 --> 00:18:36,721
Not only did you marry
without informing us...

295
00:18:36,996 --> 00:18:38,371
you brought home a pregnant wife?

296
00:18:38,971 --> 00:18:39,846
Oh my God!

297
00:18:40,055 --> 00:18:40,763
Why did he suddenly do
something so drastic?

298
00:18:40,971 --> 00:18:42,055
What the hell have you done? Stop!

299
00:18:42,138 --> 00:18:42,863
Listen to me...

300
00:18:43,013 --> 00:18:44,513
- Hit him until the broomstick breaks!
- You've ruined our reputation!

301
00:18:44,721 --> 00:18:47,638
- Come on, aunty, hit him harder!
- Enough! Stop it, please!

302
00:18:48,055 --> 00:18:49,055
- Don't interfere, sister!
- Hey, Padma, stop it.

303
00:18:49,202 --> 00:18:49,846
Hit him harder!

304
00:18:50,055 --> 00:18:50,721
Hey, enough!

305
00:18:52,138 --> 00:18:53,555
It's 80 acres of property.

306
00:18:53,888 --> 00:18:55,596
What do you think of Balanarsaiah's son?

307
00:18:55,888 --> 00:18:56,930
Well done, my boy.

308
00:18:57,263 --> 00:18:57,888
Wait, wait, wait.

309
00:18:58,096 --> 00:18:58,971
This is utter nonsense!

310
00:19:00,596 --> 00:19:02,096
How do I face people
if they ask about this?

311
00:19:02,263 --> 00:19:03,971
You're bringing shame to all of us!

312
00:19:04,263 --> 00:19:05,221
Hey, stop.

313
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,471
[indistinct chatter]
- May all evil eyes ward off.

314
00:19:07,596 --> 00:19:09,596
- Hope an heir is born soon.
- He planned something.

315
00:19:09,763 --> 00:19:11,471
[laughing]

316
00:19:11,805 --> 00:19:14,055
- Come inside. Come.
- He's taking them into the house.

317
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:15,055
Come in!

318
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:16,555
Throw that out and come in.

319
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:20,680
- Oh no!
- Hey, Padma!

320
00:19:20,888 --> 00:19:22,013
What's going on here, uncle?

321
00:19:22,346 --> 00:19:24,263
Sister, see what he's done.

322
00:19:24,555 --> 00:19:25,888
He's our only son.

323
00:19:26,305 --> 00:19:28,721
- Look what shame he's brought upon us.
- Don't cry, calm down.

324
00:19:29,013 --> 00:19:31,430
Brother,
sister-in-law is getting engaged.

325
00:19:32,430 --> 00:19:34,096
- Who the hell is he?
- Why is this happening like this?

326
00:19:34,846 --> 00:19:36,555
I planned to marry Mandu
and get the property...

327
00:19:36,763 --> 00:19:38,263
but why did my
father-in-law do this to me?

328
00:19:43,888 --> 00:19:45,471
[garbled speaking]

329
00:19:45,888 --> 00:19:46,888
[garbled speaking]

330
00:19:54,513 --> 00:19:55,471
Do you want to eat samosa?

331
00:19:56,555 --> 00:19:57,221
Wait.

332
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:58,763
- Then I'll eat.
- Carry on.

333
00:20:00,096 --> 00:20:01,221
What the hell is happening here?

334
00:20:03,888 --> 00:20:04,763
Are you groom?

335
00:20:07,763 --> 00:20:09,096
What does he have that I don't?

336
00:20:09,513 --> 00:20:10,388
Property.

337
00:20:12,346 --> 00:20:13,721
Are you a freedom fighter?

338
00:20:13,818 --> 00:20:14,568
What's with that cap?

339
00:20:17,096 --> 00:20:18,263
Wow!

340
00:20:18,763 --> 00:20:21,763
He need the oil and you
need the promotion to it.

341
00:20:21,930 --> 00:20:23,055
You managed the situation well,
didn't you?

342
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,763
Look,
you are wearing the cap as well.

343
00:20:25,971 --> 00:20:27,180
You've already got blended into them.

344
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:30,346
Father-in-law, Mandodari
can't live without me.

345
00:20:30,510 --> 00:20:31,927
She'll kill herself.
Don't destroy her life.

346
00:20:33,846 --> 00:20:34,888
Why would I die?

347
00:20:38,721 --> 00:20:39,471
Mandu.

348
00:20:43,054 --> 00:20:43,763
Mandu.

349
00:20:45,887 --> 00:20:47,220
Listen to me once.

350
00:20:48,287 --> 00:20:50,245
- Will you listen to me?
- Yes, tell me.

351
00:20:51,221 --> 00:20:52,596
Why are you doing this to me, Mandu?

352
00:20:53,971 --> 00:20:55,430
I cared for you like you were sacred.

353
00:20:56,140 --> 00:20:57,557
Did I ever touch you?

354
00:20:58,013 --> 00:20:59,805
Because you never
touched me, I'm marrying him.

355
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:04,221
You're acting arrogant
because of your beauty.

356
00:21:05,471 --> 00:21:06,346
You just watch.

357
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,638
I'll marry a girl more beautiful
than you within a week.

358
00:21:09,346 --> 00:21:11,430
You think you'll find
someone more beautiful than me?

359
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:19,930
What's going on, man?

360
00:21:20,154 --> 00:21:21,613
How long will the power be out?

361
00:21:25,888 --> 00:21:26,888
SREESHILAM DRAMA
TROUPE-"SEETHAHAPARANAM."

362
00:21:28,263 --> 00:21:31,596
In a short while, the
Sreesailam drama troupe's...

363
00:21:31,888 --> 00:21:34,263
the play "Seethapaharanam"
will begin shortly.

364
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:37,888
We request all the
villagers to come and watch.

365
00:21:42,263 --> 00:21:43,805
<i>- Alms, please.</i>
- Tell me, Malli.

366
00:21:44,055 --> 00:21:46,096
<i>- Please give alms.</i>
- Where's your friend?

367
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,055
<i>- Here, take this.</i>
- I meant...

368
00:21:48,346 --> 00:21:50,221
The girl who used to electric
shocks everyone, Damini.

369
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:52,305
<i>Then cross the line and give it to me.</i>

370
00:21:52,888 --> 00:21:56,221
<i>Otherwise, Lord Shiva's
curse will follow you, girl.</i>

371
00:21:56,430 --> 00:21:57,638
<i>- Swami that is...
- Hmm...</i>

372
00:21:58,138 --> 00:22:00,346
How much longer are we
supposed to wait? Raise the curtain!

373
00:22:00,555 --> 00:22:01,263
Hey, man.

374
00:22:01,513 --> 00:22:03,596
What is this, only dialogues
and no songs? Start the show!

375
00:22:03,846 --> 00:22:05,305
<i>Don't be so impatient. Wait, I'm coming.</i>

376
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,930
Hey everyone, are you seeing this?

377
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,596
Goddess Sita has arrived covered up.

378
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:20,263
I am Ravana, the
mighty king of Lanka!

379
00:22:21,430 --> 00:22:22,221
Hey, girl.

380
00:22:23,930 --> 00:22:26,638
Sita, you cannot escape from me.

381
00:22:30,055 --> 00:22:31,138
Hey, that's her!

382
00:22:31,888 --> 00:22:33,263
Who? Which girl do you mean?

383
00:22:33,513 --> 00:22:34,096
Oh no!

384
00:22:34,346 --> 00:22:35,555
She's the one who used to say "Oopsh!"

385
00:22:35,805 --> 00:22:37,055
Oh, Damini.

386
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:41,430
Yeah, that's Damini.

387
00:22:41,638 --> 00:22:44,680
- Don't touch her!
- Don't touch.

388
00:22:44,888 --> 00:22:45,555
Hey.

389
00:22:46,930 --> 00:22:47,930
Hey, President.

390
00:22:48,138 --> 00:22:51,971
[indistinct chatter]

391
00:22:52,388 --> 00:22:54,096
Looks like this whole crowd
are Lord Rama devotees.

392
00:22:54,513 --> 00:22:55,971
You are telling me not to touch her...

393
00:22:56,138 --> 00:22:57,680
Hey, don't go near her.

394
00:22:57,971 --> 00:22:59,013
Sita!

395
00:22:59,221 --> 00:23:03,971
Without capturing you and taking
you with me, I will not return to Lanka.

396
00:23:04,096 --> 00:23:04,888
Come!

397
00:23:04,930 --> 00:23:06,388
Hey man, don't touch the girl.

398
00:23:07,596 --> 00:23:10,930
Sita, you cannot escape from me.

399
00:23:11,471 --> 00:23:12,513
Sir!

400
00:23:13,221 --> 00:23:14,638
Look at that girl properly.

401
00:23:15,522 --> 00:23:16,647
She is Damini.

402
00:23:16,930 --> 00:23:17,638
What?

403
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:19,680
Oopsh!

404
00:23:19,796 --> 00:23:20,712
Oopsh!

405
00:23:21,013 --> 00:23:23,513
- How can I perform without touching her?
- She is Damini.

406
00:23:23,826 --> 00:23:26,784
- Our president is finished. Let's go.
- Oh no! Watch out!

407
00:23:26,933 --> 00:23:29,058
I am Ravana!
Sita, I will take you with me.

408
00:23:29,388 --> 00:23:29,930
Hey!

409
00:23:30,388 --> 00:23:31,305
Hey man!

410
00:23:35,555 --> 00:23:36,805
I kept hinting at you,
but you never understood!

411
00:23:46,388 --> 00:23:47,305
Hey, you stop!

412
00:23:47,513 --> 00:23:50,221
Hey, you coward! How did you
even become the village president?

413
00:23:59,096 --> 00:24:00,596
What is this Chandrayya,
is this how it will be?

414
00:24:00,805 --> 00:24:02,805
I let you live in our village
thinking you are one of us,

415
00:24:02,902 --> 00:24:04,904
- but your daughter doesn't care about us.
- Tell me!

416
00:24:05,181 --> 00:24:06,272
Speak up, Chandrayya! Tell me!

417
00:24:06,524 --> 00:24:08,732
He's already a coward. What would
happen if he got an electric shock.

418
00:24:09,155 --> 00:24:11,364
Do you want to live in
this village or not?

419
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,513
Why are you talking like that, President?

420
00:24:13,538 --> 00:24:15,121
You came to this unfamiliar village,
and we thought you'd live happily here.

421
00:24:15,402 --> 00:24:16,902
Why are you creating all this drama here?

422
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:21,305
Listen, Chandrayya, do you know
what your daughter did recently?

423
00:24:21,513 --> 00:24:22,346
Hey, move!

424
00:24:22,513 --> 00:24:23,805
I kept my vessel already, move!

425
00:24:23,857 --> 00:24:26,152
Hey, I kept it, can't you see?

426
00:24:27,055 --> 00:24:28,888
Huh? Electric girl. Move!

427
00:24:29,513 --> 00:24:31,680
[indistinct voices]

428
00:24:32,763 --> 00:24:33,305
- Look...
- What?

429
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:34,846
I filled the water for you.

430
00:24:35,763 --> 00:24:39,430
What oldie? You filled the water for me?

431
00:24:39,638 --> 00:24:41,555
Oh my dear!

432
00:24:42,096 --> 00:24:43,096
Mwah!

433
00:24:43,263 --> 00:24:44,971
[screams]

434
00:24:45,346 --> 00:24:45,930
Hey!

435
00:24:46,638 --> 00:24:48,096
- [voice muted]
- Ah? Oh no!

436
00:24:49,346 --> 00:24:50,596
Come on, look at him.

437
00:24:50,805 --> 00:24:52,263
This TV was gifted by my mother.

438
00:24:52,555 --> 00:24:53,846
I'm not going to keep silent anymore.

439
00:24:54,418 --> 00:24:56,668
Hey! Why are you taking it so seriously?

440
00:24:56,771 --> 00:24:58,271
It's just your TV that got broken.

441
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:00,471
Our president's health
is completely ruined.

442
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:01,263
You idiot!

443
00:25:01,888 --> 00:25:03,346
Why are you making
fun of me, Balamani?

444
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,471
There's nothing wrong
with me. Stop insulting me.

445
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:08,846
What was the need
for her to get on stage?

446
00:25:09,077 --> 00:25:09,619
What need?

447
00:25:10,888 --> 00:25:13,971
I stepped onto the stage to show my
talent because nobody recognizes me.

448
00:25:14,142 --> 00:25:15,267
What now?
Oopsh!

449
00:25:15,846 --> 00:25:17,471
- Doesn't anyone recognize you?
- Yeah.

450
00:25:17,763 --> 00:25:18,930
- Hey, Lachi.
- Yes, sir.

451
00:25:19,138 --> 00:25:21,680
Put up the posters I printed
for this girl all over the village.

452
00:25:21,888 --> 00:25:22,846
- Okay, sir.
- That's it.

453
00:25:23,138 --> 00:25:24,596
Not just the village, paste
them across the whole district.

454
00:25:24,805 --> 00:25:26,013
Everyone will recognize
you from now on.

455
00:25:26,471 --> 00:25:27,680
Isn't this the
recognition you wanted?

456
00:25:28,471 --> 00:25:30,638
Your daughter's stunt
yesterday nearly killed us.

457
00:25:31,263 --> 00:25:32,888
- What's your problem, people?
- [all]: Oh no!

458
00:25:33,346 --> 00:25:36,096
- Wait, dear. I'll talk to them.
- You stay back, dad!

459
00:25:36,889 --> 00:25:38,763
Tell me, whose life was ruined here?

460
00:25:38,808 --> 00:25:39,850
Everyone looks perfectly fine, right?

461
00:25:40,305 --> 00:25:42,430
When the groom's family
came to see Saritha...

462
00:25:42,897 --> 00:25:43,897
your daughter gave me
an electric shock,

463
00:25:43,922 --> 00:25:46,603
and the groom's family ran away
after seeing us like that.

464
00:25:49,930 --> 00:25:51,388
I don't think this meeting
will end anytime soon.

465
00:25:51,462 --> 00:25:53,129
- I'm leaving. Oops!
- Hey, move aside.

466
00:25:55,789 --> 00:25:58,238
Looks like no wedding will happen
in this village until she gets married.

467
00:25:58,596 --> 00:26:01,221
Yes, Chandrayya! The
groom's family came yesterday...

468
00:26:01,246 --> 00:26:01,871
to see your daughter,
right? What happened?

469
00:26:02,328 --> 00:26:03,370
What should I say?

470
00:26:09,513 --> 00:26:10,555
Come on, let's leave. Move.

471
00:26:10,659 --> 00:26:12,367
- Let me speak to him and come back.
- Come on, let's leave.

472
00:26:12,506 --> 00:26:14,173
Meeting's done. He'll handle
the remaining matters, now move.

473
00:26:14,417 --> 00:26:16,167
Chandrayya, if you don't mind...

474
00:26:16,555 --> 00:26:18,721
I'll tell you something from
my general knowledge. Listen.

475
00:26:18,888 --> 00:26:20,638
Everyone in the village is
suffering because of your daughter.

476
00:26:20,846 --> 00:26:22,888
If another marriage
proposal comes, don't miss it.

477
00:26:24,221 --> 00:26:26,263
Hey, you seem to have
a lot of knowledge...

478
00:26:26,555 --> 00:26:29,805
Even after the warning, you
touched her on stage and got shocked.

479
00:26:30,013 --> 00:26:31,013
I thought people were clapping.

480
00:26:31,750 --> 00:26:33,584
- That's why I called you a coward.
- Okay, let's go home.

481
00:26:33,661 --> 00:26:34,703
Let's go.

482
00:26:36,125 --> 00:26:38,208
Uncle, she looks better
than Mandu, right?

483
00:26:38,250 --> 00:26:39,291
I should show her.

484
00:26:39,416 --> 00:26:40,583
Obviously she does!

485
00:26:40,625 --> 00:26:41,625
Come with me, I'll show you.

486
00:26:41,958 --> 00:26:44,041
Bad time's about to
start. Drive faster, brother.

487
00:26:55,666 --> 00:26:57,375
You useless idiot!

488
00:26:57,583 --> 00:26:59,458
This is a laddu, not a samosa, brother.

489
00:27:03,875 --> 00:27:05,458
Move your legs a little, please.

490
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:08,757
Where is the bride?

491
00:27:08,973 --> 00:27:10,723
She has gone to the beauty parlor.

492
00:27:11,125 --> 00:27:13,208
She'll be back in five
minutes. Please sit down.

493
00:27:14,666 --> 00:27:15,666
Why is she sweeping now?

494
00:27:17,375 --> 00:27:18,208
Lower your legs.

495
00:27:23,589 --> 00:27:24,506
She looks good!

496
00:27:25,859 --> 00:27:27,078
Is the make-up done?

497
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:28,061
Yes, it's done.

498
00:27:29,958 --> 00:27:32,375
Girl, looks like the
make-up wore off a bit.

499
00:27:32,450 --> 00:27:33,742
Oh God! Really, uncle?

500
00:27:35,239 --> 00:27:36,823
That's true. Wait a moment.

501
00:27:37,054 --> 00:27:39,547
I'll go to the parlor, get my make-up
done again, and come back. Bye.

502
