at your house again today?

757
00:42:09,286 --> 00:42:10,869
Want some ice cream?

758
00:42:12,411 --> 00:42:13,911
Okay, wait. I'll get you some ice cream.

759
00:42:14,619 --> 00:42:16,036
Hey, stop!

760
00:42:27,286 --> 00:42:28,078
What's wrong?

761
00:42:32,994 --> 00:42:34,619
I gave him an electric shock!

762
00:42:37,536 --> 00:42:40,161
Dear baby, do you
want ice cream too?

763
00:42:40,661 --> 00:42:44,036
No, the three of us will have it
together after you're born.

764
00:42:45,286 --> 00:42:47,161
These days, they say
women in Rajasthan are...

765
00:42:47,369 --> 00:42:49,328
having only baby girls
in their first delivery!

766
00:42:49,578 --> 00:42:50,578
Leave those newspaper stories aside!

767
00:42:50,786 --> 00:42:52,536
Focus on Yadagiri's marriage first.

768
00:42:52,786 --> 00:42:54,953
Unemployed, yet fully booked
with the daily news.

769
00:42:54,994 --> 00:42:57,119
It would be better if you
toned down that arrogance.

770
00:42:57,369 --> 00:42:58,328
Who's being arrogant?

771
00:42:58,744 --> 00:42:59,703
Is it you or me?

772
00:42:59,953 --> 00:43:01,619
- Hey, it's you!
- Hey, stop it.

773
00:43:01,869 --> 00:43:02,953
- Hey, leave it!
- Hey!

774
00:43:03,161 --> 00:43:04,744
He started this early in the morning!

775
00:43:06,244 --> 00:43:07,911
You're having big daydreams.

776
00:43:08,953 --> 00:43:10,369
We fought when we had nothing.

777
00:43:10,828 --> 00:43:12,453
Even now, we're
fighting for those 80 acres,

778
00:43:12,581 --> 00:43:13,998
without knowing if
they'll belong to us or not.

779
00:43:15,494 --> 00:43:16,578
Remember how we used to be?

780
00:43:16,869 --> 00:43:17,869
What have we turned into now?

781
00:43:18,851 --> 00:43:20,143
What is this, Balanarsu?

782
00:43:20,536 --> 00:43:23,203
We have an engagement tomorrow
morning. Why this fight now?

783
00:43:23,411 --> 00:43:24,203
What is it, sister-in-law?

784
00:43:24,296 --> 00:43:25,953
Do you think this is a fight?

785
00:43:26,369 --> 00:43:28,578
Did you even tell me about this alliance?

786
00:43:29,744 --> 00:43:31,078
Sister already told you.

787
00:43:31,369 --> 00:43:33,119
You walked away without hearing her out.

788
00:43:33,369 --> 00:43:34,661
Hey, just keep quiet.

789
00:43:35,911 --> 00:43:36,828
She always gets involved!

790
00:43:36,853 --> 00:43:37,728
Why are you so angry?

791
00:43:38,067 --> 00:43:39,109
Why are you scolding your wife?

792
00:43:39,369 --> 00:43:40,703
Won't you listen to me?

793
00:43:40,911 --> 00:43:42,953
Look, sister-in-law...
who will listen to you?

794
00:43:43,536 --> 00:43:44,536
Brother won't listen to you.

795
00:43:47,078 --> 00:43:48,494
Yadagiri doesn't care at all.

796
00:43:48,786 --> 00:43:50,369
Then why do you think
I'll listen to you?

797
00:43:51,536 --> 00:43:53,828
Forget the engagement.
We won't come.

798
00:43:54,036 --> 00:43:55,161
That's final.

799
00:43:57,536 --> 00:43:58,286
Yadhi...

800
00:43:58,703 --> 00:43:59,786
Tell me.
What is it?

801
00:44:00,036 --> 00:44:04,328
Can you put the ring on tomorrow
without even touching me?

802
00:44:06,078 --> 00:44:06,744
Uncle.

803
00:44:09,203 --> 00:44:09,994
What's with this girl?

804
00:44:10,328 --> 00:44:12,036
She wants me to put the engagement
ring on her without touching her.

805
00:44:12,161 --> 00:44:12,994
Oh...

806
00:44:13,078 --> 00:44:14,494
You never touched
anyone until now, right?

807
00:44:14,744 --> 00:44:17,453
So that means she's
a traditional girl like you.

808
00:44:18,994 --> 00:44:19,703
Yadhi!

809
00:44:20,703 --> 00:44:21,494
Hello! Hello!

810
00:44:22,203 --> 00:44:23,161
What is it now?

811
00:44:23,411 --> 00:44:25,203
You want me to put the engagement ring
on you without touching you. Right?

812
00:44:26,244 --> 00:44:27,744
- Yes.
- Okay, let's do that.

813
00:44:29,494 --> 00:44:30,286
Is it?

814
00:44:31,078 --> 00:44:32,161
Yes.

815
00:44:32,322 --> 00:44:33,280
Is it?

816
00:44:35,078 --> 00:44:36,036
Yes.

817
00:44:37,453 --> 00:44:38,494
Uncle.

818
00:44:39,078 --> 00:44:42,203
Once my marriage is done,
I'll find a bride for you as well.

819
00:44:43,869 --> 00:44:45,203
Why do I need marriage so early?

820
00:44:45,869 --> 00:44:47,869
[both laughing]

821
00:44:48,578 --> 00:44:50,578
[in unison]: Uncle,
one photograph, please!

822
00:45:10,659 --> 00:45:15,284
[Priest reciting wedding chants]

823
00:45:23,119 --> 00:45:25,578
I assume everyone
from the groom's family has arrived?

824
00:45:26,119 --> 00:45:27,661
Is Bala Narasaiah coming or not?

825
00:45:27,686 --> 00:45:28,727
[horn honking]

826
00:45:36,328 --> 00:45:38,203
- Greetings, brother-in-law. Please come.
- Brother!

827
00:45:41,494 --> 00:45:42,453
- Please come in, brother-in-law.
- Welcome...

828
00:45:42,569 --> 00:45:44,485
- Don't mind. I got a little late.
- It's alright!

829
00:45:52,015 --> 00:45:53,057
What did you say
to actually make him show up?

830
00:45:53,930 --> 00:45:55,721
You'll get 80 acres anyway.

831
00:45:56,369 --> 00:45:57,911
This is the final wedding in our family.

832
00:45:58,161 --> 00:45:59,328
We aren't outsiders, are we?

833
00:45:59,634 --> 00:46:02,384
After all, it is a blood relationship,
how could you not come?

834
00:46:02,736 --> 00:46:04,319
He's your older brother.

835
00:46:04,344 --> 00:46:06,052
He'll always stand by you.

836
00:46:08,953 --> 00:46:09,869
That's nice!

837
00:46:11,661 --> 00:46:13,578
Brother, your brother has come.

838
00:46:13,828 --> 00:46:15,203
He loves you a lot.

839
00:46:18,161 --> 00:46:19,786
Excuse me, give the rings.

840
00:46:40,328 --> 00:46:41,411
What kind of rings are these?

841
00:46:42,244 --> 00:46:46,661
What is this, priest? These rings
are made from Karungali tree roots.

842
00:46:46,807 --> 00:46:50,890
We've been following this tradition of
using these rings since our forefathers.

843
00:46:51,204 --> 00:46:53,746
We believe that the relationship
between a girl and a boy...

844
00:46:54,154 --> 00:46:57,446
...will be as strong as the
roots of the Karungali tree.

845
00:46:57,536 --> 00:47:00,244
Priest, let's use these rings for today.

846
00:47:00,408 --> 00:47:02,199
From tomorrow, you use
your rings and we'll use ours.

847
00:47:02,453 --> 00:47:03,578
- Okay?
- Alright, sir.

848
00:47:06,411 --> 00:47:07,744
Were these made from tree roots?

849
00:47:08,494 --> 00:47:09,536
So it won't cause a shock.

850
00:47:09,953 --> 00:47:11,411
- It won't shock.
- It won't shock.

851
00:47:11,619 --> 00:47:12,286
It won't shock.

852
00:47:12,494 --> 00:47:14,703
- He says it won't shock.
- He says it won't shock.

853
00:47:14,953 --> 00:47:16,744
- He says it won't shock.
- It won't shock.

854
00:47:17,119 --> 00:47:18,619
Coward! You said it out loud!

855
00:47:18,828 --> 00:47:20,328
- What do you mean, shock?
- I mean...

856
00:47:20,619 --> 00:47:22,328
Knife! It's a new knife!

857
00:47:25,078 --> 00:47:27,369
I cut the fruit using a new knife.

858
00:47:29,244 --> 00:47:30,036
It's a new knife.

859
00:47:30,286 --> 00:47:32,703
We like such traditions.
This is what we want.

860
00:47:32,953 --> 00:47:34,119
Begin the music.

861
00:47:34,619 --> 00:47:35,786
Exchange the rings.

862
00:48:05,244 --> 00:48:06,578
[In Tamil]: Hurry up, we're getting late.

863
00:48:07,453 --> 00:48:08,661
Oh Lord Murugesha!

864
00:48:08,869 --> 00:48:09,953
You idiot!

865
00:48:10,203 --> 00:48:11,203
- Hey!
- Who is he?

866
00:48:11,494 --> 00:48:12,369
He is Paralokam Pradeep.

867
00:48:12,786 --> 00:48:14,369
He's a still photographer
from Chennai.

868
00:48:14,744 --> 00:48:17,536
Hey Balamani, I got him from Chennai.
We don't want local people for this.

869
00:48:18,786 --> 00:48:19,994
Everybody, smile please!

870
00:48:20,328 --> 00:48:20,994
Look here.

871
00:48:21,536 --> 00:48:22,369
Madam.

872
00:48:23,244 --> 00:48:24,744
Please smile. Smile...

873
00:48:27,703 --> 00:48:29,119
Take those rings off.

874
00:48:29,411 --> 00:48:30,578
- I'll give you new rings.
- What?

875
00:48:30,786 --> 00:48:31,536
What did he just say?

876
00:48:32,744 --> 00:48:33,203
Take this.

877
00:48:33,494 --> 00:48:34,536
- Hey!
- Use these instead!

878
00:48:35,661 --> 00:48:36,786
What's gotten into you!?

879
00:48:37,161 --> 00:48:38,911
Once the bride and groom
have exchanged rings,

880
00:48:39,078 --> 00:48:41,078
how can you replace them with
new rings, ignoring their tradition?

881
00:48:41,161 --> 00:48:44,244
What about the custom they've
been following since their ancestors?

882
00:48:44,369 --> 00:48:46,869
[in Tamil]: I don't understand
what you're saying, madam.

883
00:48:47,036 --> 00:48:49,328
- Oh, you want poori?
- Poori?

884
00:48:49,536 --> 00:48:51,869
He wants poori. Give him
some pooris. Move aside.

885
00:48:52,661 --> 00:48:56,328
- What is this, Mahesh?
- Oh, you want potatoes.

886
00:48:56,536 --> 00:48:58,411
- Alright, let's go.
- Give him some potato curry!

887
00:48:58,578 --> 00:49:00,453
Tomorrow is the
pre-wedding shoot. Be ready.

888
00:49:00,661 --> 00:49:02,578
He's asking for beer.

889
00:49:02,786 --> 00:49:03,619
- We'll take care of it.
- Sir!

890
00:49:03,703 --> 00:49:05,578
- Priest, you continue.
- You people continue!

891
00:49:16,036 --> 00:49:16,828
Yadhi!

892
00:49:17,494 --> 00:49:19,953
Do we really need
the pre-wedding shoot now?

893
00:49:20,328 --> 00:49:22,036
It's not like we'll do this repeatedly,
right? It happens only once in my life.

894
00:49:22,369 --> 00:49:23,244
Please don't talk like that.

895
00:49:23,703 --> 00:49:25,203
- That is...
- I'm here for you, right? I'll handle it.

896
00:49:25,411 --> 00:49:26,744
Oh God!

897
00:49:26,911 --> 00:49:28,661
Madam, a simple pose.

898
00:49:29,119 --> 00:49:33,286
If you make your fingers
like this... it's a love symbol.

899
00:49:33,578 --> 00:49:34,453
Hey!

900
00:49:34,661 --> 00:49:36,536
Is that so? Fine, do it!

901
00:49:37,036 --> 00:49:38,661
Just hold on, madam.

902
00:49:38,994 --> 00:49:40,869
- Wait! Wait! Wait!
- This isn't happening today!

903
00:49:41,078 --> 00:49:41,911
What's wrong with you!?

904
00:49:42,161 --> 00:49:44,244
You don't know how to do it properly.

905
00:49:44,661 --> 00:49:46,786
Do it properly.
Wait! Wait! Wait!

906
00:49:47,453 --> 00:49:49,536
Why are you bending
your fingers like that?

907
00:49:52,328 --> 00:49:53,328
Change the costume.

908
00:49:53,449 --> 00:49:54,199
So soon?

909
00:49:58,578 --> 00:50:00,661
"Marigold... Chrysanthemum..."

910
00:50:02,286 --> 00:50:04,203
How can you both kiss before marriage!?

911
00:50:04,328 --> 00:50:05,036
He's responsible for this!

912
00:50:05,119 --> 00:50:07,869
You'll go straight to heaven, Pradeep.

913
00:50:09,161 --> 00:50:11,453
Madam, now most important shot.

914
00:50:12,286 --> 00:50:15,244
- Titanic Pose.
- What's a Titanic pose means?

915
00:50:31,328 --> 00:50:32,036
Uncle.

916
00:50:32,328 --> 00:50:33,161
Oh no!

917
00:50:33,369 --> 00:50:35,036
- Uncle! Uncle!
- Yes, that pose looks good!

918
00:50:35,161 --> 00:50:36,828
I want to tell you something.

919
00:50:37,078 --> 00:50:39,078
- Nice hairstyle.
- Not that.

920
00:50:39,703 --> 00:50:40,786
I got a shock when I touched her.

921
00:50:41,036 --> 00:50:43,828
- Is it true?
- Why would I lie to you? It's true.

922
00:50:45,411 --> 00:50:45,994
Hey!

923
00:50:46,786 --> 00:50:50,494
In Magadheera, Ram Charan also got
an electric shock when he touched Kajal.

924
00:50:50,828 --> 00:50:53,411
- Yours is a bond across many lifetimes.
- Yes, brother!

925
00:50:53,661 --> 00:50:58,953
Then I must be Bhairava
and she must be Mitravinda!

926
00:50:59,244 --> 00:51:02,036
[squealing]

927
00:51:02,203 --> 00:51:04,078
Pradeep, you're going to die now.

928
00:51:04,328 --> 00:51:05,703
You don't know about that girl.

929
00:51:05,953 --> 00:51:07,703
[in Tamil]: Who the hell are you?

930
00:51:08,286 --> 00:51:08,994
Ready, madam?

931
00:51:09,453 --> 00:51:11,536
You splash the water, and
I'll click the photo. Okay?

932
00:51:14,161 --> 00:51:17,203
One, two, three.

933
00:51:19,161 --> 00:51:20,203
Oh no!

934
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:21,744
He deserved it!

935
00:51:40,203 --> 00:51:40,994
Hello.

936
00:51:41,100 --> 00:51:44,142
Damini, I found out the truth about you.

937
00:51:45,702 --> 00:51:46,785
I want to talk to you. I'm coming.

938
00:51:47,244 --> 00:51:48,369
Yadhi, what happened?

939
00:51:50,411 --> 00:51:53,828
[gasps]
Oh no!

940
00:51:59,328 --> 00:52:00,453
I think he got to know.

941
00:52:04,911 --> 00:52:07,661
Father is also not
at home at this time.

942
00:52:13,244 --> 00:52:14,328
Damini.

943
00:52:15,284 --> 00:52:17,076
Yadhi, what happened?

944
00:52:19,136 --> 00:52:20,344
What happened?

945
00:52:20,911 --> 00:52:22,453
Look straight into my eyes.

946
00:52:25,369 --> 00:52:26,286
I can't see.

947
00:52:27,494 --> 00:52:28,703
I came to know a truth.

948
00:52:30,078 --> 00:52:30,828
What truth is that?

949
00:52:35,828 --> 00:52:38,244
Ours is a bond that lasts
across lifetimes. My uncle told me.

950
00:52:39,453 --> 00:52:41,119
Bond that lasts across lifetimes?

951
00:52:45,119 --> 00:52:47,661
Yadhi, I thought the same.

952
00:52:49,244 --> 00:52:51,536
- Damini.
- Did you come to tell this?

953
00:52:52,286 --> 00:52:53,328
Is there no one at home?

954
00:52:53,619 --> 00:52:55,994
Yes but why?

955
00:52:56,953 --> 00:53:00,119
I mean...

956
00:53:00,369 --> 00:53:05,286
Yadhi, we decided not to touch
each other until we get married.

957
00:53:05,311 --> 00:53:06,644
Our engagement is done, right?

958
00:53:06,924 --> 00:53:08,132
That means half the marriage is done.

959
00:53:08,578 --> 00:53:10,244
- So?
- There's nothing wrong with it.

960
00:53:10,578 --> 00:53:11,411
Please.

961
00:53:12,869 --> 00:53:15,328
No, Yadhi, I said no.

962
00:53:21,994 --> 00:53:22,828
Damini.

963
00:53:27,828 --> 00:53:29,328
Son-in-law, is that you?

964
00:53:30,286 --> 00:53:31,744
When did you arrive?

965
00:53:31,994 --> 00:53:33,161
- Just now, father-in-law.
- Oh!

966
00:53:34,078 --> 00:53:35,119
You came without informing me.

967
00:53:36,244 --> 00:53:38,453
I came to see how the
wedding preparations are going.

968
00:53:38,828 --> 00:53:40,286
Marriage preparations?

969
00:53:40,869 --> 00:53:42,244
- This is your house, right?
- Please sit.

970
00:53:42,994 --> 00:53:44,078
Please sit.

971
00:53:48,578 --> 00:53:49,994
Would you like to have tea or coffee?

972
00:53:51,411 --> 00:53:52,119
I'll ask for tea.

973
00:53:53,244 --> 00:53:55,036
Dear, bring tea for our son-in-law.

974
00:53:55,244 --> 00:53:56,119
<i>Okay, Dad!</i>

975
00:53:57,536 --> 00:54:00,619
I want to tell you something, son-in-law.

976
00:54:00,994 --> 00:54:01,828
Tell me, father-in-law.

977
00:54:02,744 --> 00:54:06,328
I wanted to tell you
something for a long time.

978
00:54:06,911 --> 00:54:07,744
But I couldn't.

979
00:54:09,078 --> 00:54:11,494
Actually... Son-in-law...

980
00:54:12,661 --> 00:54:18,536
I told my people as well...
There's a small issue with my daughter.

981
00:54:20,244 --> 00:54:23,578
Sometimes she gives electric shocks
when we touch her.

982
00:54:25,703 --> 00:54:26,744
Is that so?

983
00:54:30,286 --> 00:54:32,661
Son-in-law, I'm telling you this
because I hope you understand.

984
00:54:33,078 --> 00:54:36,036
Other than this, she is a very nice girl.

985
00:54:37,078 --> 00:54:41,494
If you can accept this,
we'll be fortunate.

986
00:55:00,286 --> 00:55:01,953
- Oh no, son-in-law!
- Tell me, father-in-law.

987
00:55:02,953 --> 00:55:05,536
- Bag.
- Sorry, this is your bag, right?

988
00:55:05,744 --> 00:55:08,036
I've told you everything about Damini.

989
00:55:08,203 --> 00:55:08,828
Sorry, father-in-law.

990
00:55:09,286 --> 00:55:10,286
Don't mind.

991
00:55:10,536 --> 00:55:12,119
I didn't catch what you said.

992
00:55:12,411 --> 00:55:14,744
- You didn't hear me?
- My mind was somewhere else.

993
00:55:15,744 --> 00:55:17,036
We'll talk about it another time.

994
00:55:19,494 --> 00:55:20,953
It seems like you're ready for marriage.

995
00:55:21,953 --> 00:55:22,869
Bye, father-in-law.

996
00:55:43,828 --> 00:55:48,786
"Yadhi's wedding has the whole village
buzzing, but the girl is delicate."

997
00:55:50,578 --> 00:55:52,286
"The groom is a miser.

998
00:55:52,494 --> 00:55:55,619
"This boy has a lifelong warranty."

999
00:55:57,494 --> 00:56:01,494
"Oh, happy days are here!"

1000
00:56:02,244 --> 00:56:05,536
"Our families have become one."

1001
00:56:05,869 --> 00:56:08,578
"There's no one else to touch you."

1002
00:56:13,619 --> 00:56:14,578
DAMINI WEDS YADHAGIRI.

1003
00:56:43,828 --> 00:56:46,661
We made the matchmaking a hit,
the engagement a super hit.

1004
00:56:46,911 --> 00:56:49,578
Sister, the marriage
is nearly done. Mission successful.

1005
00:56:50,244 --> 00:56:51,828
[crowd]: We're gonna smash
all odds and get her married!

1006
00:56:52,119 --> 00:56:54,119
- [crowd]:
- We're gonna
smash all odds and get her married!

1007
00:56:54,661 --> 00:56:56,703
[in Hindi]: Hey, wait a minute.

1008
00:56:56,800 --> 00:56:57,842
[in Hindi]: Have some patience.

1009
00:56:58,828 --> 00:57:02,161
The real story has just started.

1010
00:57:43,953 --> 00:57:49,328
"Yadhi's wedding has the whole village
buzzing, but the girl is delicate."

1011
00:57:50,828 --> 00:57:52,494
"The groom is a miser."

1012
00:57:52,786 --> 00:57:55,953
"The boy has talent
and the girl has current."

1013
00:58:01,744 --> 00:58:03,661
Ma'am, bring the nuptial chain.

1014
00:58:06,119 --> 00:58:11,036
[Priest reciting marriage chants]

1015
00:58:25,453 --> 00:58:26,786
Start the percussion’s.

1016
00:58:28,578 --> 00:58:34,494
[Priest reciting marriage chants]

1017
00:58:58,494 --> 00:59:04,411
[gasps]
[Priest reciting marriage chants]

1018
00:59:07,369 --> 00:59:09,703
Uncle, come here, I got a shock again.

1019
00:59:09,776 --> 00:59:10,817
- You got a shock again?
- Yes.

1020
00:59:11,036 --> 00:59:13,536
Magadheera, Ram Charan, Kajal.

1021
00:59:13,828 --> 00:59:15,161
You guys are destined to be together.

1022
00:59:16,744 --> 00:59:17,953
Hey, you idiot.

1023
00:59:18,203 --> 00:59:20,494
How many times do I have to tell you
not to throw the wires like that?

1024
00:59:20,703 --> 00:59:21,953
- Look, he got a shock again.
- Wires?

1025
00:59:22,286 --> 00:59:24,453
- Get up! Move from there.
- It seems he is a wireless photographer.

1026
00:59:24,911 --> 00:59:25,911
Move!

1027
00:59:30,078 --> 00:59:35,453
[Priest reciting marriage chants]

1028
00:59:37,911 --> 00:59:40,036
- Yea! The wedding is completed.
- Hey! Hey!

1029
00:59:40,244 --> 00:59:41,869
- The wedding is finish!
- Hey, hey...

1030
00:59:42,244 --> 00:59:43,744
- Hey, wait...
- The wedding is completed.

1031
00:59:44,244 --> 00:59:45,078
Marriage isn't completed yet...

1032
00:59:45,244 --> 00:59:48,328
The groom and the bride should take
seven rounds before the holy fire, right?

1033
00:59:48,536 --> 00:59:51,994
Oh, coward! How can he catch her finger?

1034
00:59:52,661 --> 00:59:54,244
The sacred knot has to be tied.
Come, get up.

1035
01:01:12,619 --> 01:01:15,203
He isn't getting shocked,
looks like son-in-law is stronger.

1036
01:01:15,453 --> 01:01:16,661
Good choice.

1037
01:01:19,453 --> 01:01:20,453
Sir, sir, sir. Hold still.

1038
01:01:26,119 --> 01:01:28,078
"Here comes the star"

1039
01:01:29,744 --> 01:01:32,578
"Turn and see!"

1040
01:01:32,994 --> 01:01:34,911
"Don't go after her"

1041
01:02:07,911 --> 01:02:10,078
Wow! What a step son-in-law.

1042
01:02:41,828 --> 01:02:42,661
Dad...

1043
01:02:44,828 --> 01:02:46,328
- Did you tell him?
- I will tell him.

1044
01:02:46,619 --> 01:02:48,203
- You sit inside.
- Please tell him.

1045
01:02:48,619 --> 01:02:49,619
Tell him.

1046
01:02:50,536 --> 01:02:52,328
- Uncle, it's urgent.
- Control for sometime.

1047
01:02:52,703 --> 01:02:53,619
- Control it.
- Son-in-law.

1048
01:02:54,036 --> 01:02:55,828
I need to tell you something,
come with me.

1049
01:03:02,036 --> 01:03:06,328
Son-in-law, I've been trying
to tell you something for a long time.

1050
01:03:06,536 --> 01:03:08,494
I know what you want
to tell me, father-in-law.

1051
01:03:10,286 --> 01:03:11,286
She is your only daughter,

1052
01:03:11,578 --> 01:03:13,578
you raised her very fondly,
she is a motherless child,

1053
01:03:14,744 --> 01:03:17,286
I have to take care of her,
isn't it father-in-law?

1054
01:03:18,786 --> 01:03:20,369
Don't worry, father-in-law.
I'll take care of it.

1055
01:03:21,161 --> 01:03:22,703
I want to tell you
something else, son-in-law.

1056
01:03:23,369 --> 01:03:24,328
Tell me, father-in-law.

1057
01:03:26,411 --> 01:03:27,536
Son-in-law...

1058
01:03:27,828 --> 01:03:30,869
I don't have the courage to look
into your eyes and tell you.

1059
01:03:31,078 --> 01:03:34,203
- No one will look at me, right?
- My daughter has a small problem.

1060
01:03:35,369 --> 01:03:37,869
The doctors said
there is no treatment for it.

1061
01:03:39,453 --> 01:03:41,203
You will get a shock if you touch her.

1062
01:03:42,578 --> 01:03:45,286
Now I'm putting my child in your hands.

1063
01:03:45,578 --> 01:03:49,036
- Oh no!
- You have to take care of her.

1064
01:03:49,136 --> 01:03:51,471
I know, father-in-law.
You don't worry, I will take care of her.

1065
01:03:53,078 --> 01:03:54,703
- My wonderful son-in-law.
- Yes, father-in-law.

1066
01:03:55,828 --> 01:03:57,203
I'm relieved.

1067
01:03:57,619 --> 01:03:59,036
- Let's go, son-in-law.
- Okay, father-in-law.

1068
01:04:00,161 --> 01:04:01,869
I've told everything to son-in-law.

1069
01:04:03,036 --> 01:04:04,244
Don't worry.

1070
01:04:07,786 --> 01:04:08,369
Bye, dear.

1071
01:04:09,203 --> 01:04:10,786
- Bye, son-in-law.
- See you, dad.

1072
01:04:11,953 --> 01:04:12,994
Bye, dad.

1073
01:05:12,286 --> 01:05:13,911
Sister, look there.

1074
01:05:19,619 --> 01:05:21,369
Stop, man. Stop it!

1075
01:05:39,786 --> 01:05:42,578
- He's...
- Will he send it to son-in-law or what?

1076
01:05:43,369 --> 01:05:44,703
Attack!

1077
01:05:53,619 --> 01:05:54,703
[in Tamil]: Leave me.

1078
01:06:21,786 --> 01:06:23,619
Hey, read this.

1079
01:06:26,369 --> 01:06:27,578
Read. Read it.

1080
01:06:27,869 --> 01:06:29,994
I can't read, I am uneducated.

1081
01:06:30,744 --> 01:06:32,286
[in Tamil]: Give this to your brother.

1082
01:06:32,578 --> 01:06:33,994
Your brother? Brother...

1083
01:06:34,911 --> 01:06:37,161
- Oh, brother Yadhi?
- [in Tamil]: Yes, give it to him.

1084
01:06:37,411 --> 01:06:38,744
I'll give it to him.

1085
01:06:51,244 --> 01:06:52,119
<i>Brother.</i>

1086
01:06:55,036 --> 01:06:56,953
- Where did you go?
- Here, take it, brother.

1087
01:06:58,244 --> 01:06:59,369
What's this paper?

1088
01:06:59,619 --> 01:07:00,786
The photographer gave it to me.

1089
01:07:00,994 --> 01:07:03,494
Brother... Give me money, brother.

1090
01:07:04,078 --> 01:07:06,161
I will celebrate, brother.

1091
01:07:08,786 --> 01:07:09,703
Thank you, brother.

1092
01:07:13,411 --> 01:07:14,453
<i>Hey, Yadhi.</i>

1093
01:07:24,369 --> 01:07:30,828
Hit it! Hit it! Do it!

1094
01:07:30,869 --> 01:07:32,869
Yeah! Yeah!

1095
01:07:33,119 --> 01:07:34,619
- It's time...
- All the best, man.

1096
01:07:35,244 --> 01:07:36,161
All the best.

1097
01:07:37,494 --> 01:07:41,453
[Telugu song playing in the background]

1098
01:09:10,869 --> 01:09:12,869
[groans]

1099
01:09:14,744 --> 01:09:15,869
Oh no!

1100
01:09:21,536 --> 01:09:22,369
Hey, Yadhi.

1101
01:09:35,744 --> 01:09:37,494
[both screaming]

1102
01:09:51,453 --> 01:09:52,411
Hey, Yadhi.

1103
01:09:53,328 --> 01:09:54,453
Take some time...

1104
01:09:54,703 --> 01:09:56,244
The shouting is clearly audible.

1105
01:09:58,911 --> 01:10:00,869
[in Hindi]:
Take two minutes of break, man.

1106
01:10:41,328 --> 01:10:43,994
OH..! SUKUMARI

1107
01:10:58,856 --> 01:11:01,106
Mother-in-law, give it to me.
I'll cut it.

1108
01:11:01,856 --> 01:11:02,522
It's okay, dear.

1109
01:11:02,814 --> 01:11:04,022
Give some tea to Yadhi.

1110
01:11:10,272 --> 01:11:12,564
Sister,
is it true that Yadhi broke the cot...

1111
01:11:16,231 --> 01:11:20,064
- Oh no!
- Hey, keep quiet.

1112
01:11:20,314 --> 01:11:21,647
How would I know she is here.

1113
01:11:29,106 --> 01:11:30,272
Your brother-in-law is good for nothing.

1114
01:11:30,814 --> 01:11:32,564
Forget breaking the cot,

1115
01:11:32,856 --> 01:11:34,481
he can't even move it.

1116
01:11:34,606 --> 01:11:37,064
Oh no! How can you talk so shamelessly?

1117
01:11:37,231 --> 01:11:38,356
What do you want me to do?

1118
01:11:38,731 --> 01:11:40,606
Everyone is talking about Yadhi.

1119
01:11:40,689 --> 01:11:43,314
- The whole village is talking about him.
- Oh no! Stop now!

1120
01:11:47,564 --> 01:11:48,397
Dear, tea.

1121
01:11:55,439 --> 01:11:57,439
The new groom is going somewhere!

1122
01:11:57,606 --> 01:11:58,647
What, Yadhi?

1123
01:11:58,731 --> 01:12:00,231
Is it true you broke the cot?

1124
01:12:00,397 --> 01:12:01,981
You take after your grandfather.

1125
01:12:03,022 --> 01:12:04,231
How do you know about my grandfather?

1126
01:12:04,481 --> 01:12:05,314
Well...

1127
01:12:05,606 --> 01:12:08,022
- Once...
- Oh God!

1128
01:12:08,231 --> 01:12:10,106
By the way, what happened to your hair?

1129
01:12:10,856 --> 01:12:11,897
This hairstyle? My wife did it.

1130
01:12:12,106 --> 01:12:13,439
- Does it look nice?
- Oh ho!

1131
01:12:16,397 --> 01:12:18,272
Oh no! My back is stiff.

1132
01:12:28,856 --> 01:12:30,939
Can you put the ring
without touching me?

1133
01:12:33,481 --> 01:12:34,897
"Who is that guy?"

1134
01:12:35,939 --> 01:12:37,397
"He is Damini's husband."

1135
01:12:37,897 --> 01:12:38,981
Oh ho!

1136
01:12:39,272 --> 01:12:40,647
"Is he Damini's husband?"

1137
01:12:41,439 --> 01:12:43,147
"Yes, he is."

1138
01:12:43,439 --> 01:12:45,022
"Good choice... Good choice."

1139
01:12:46,106 --> 01:12:47,147
"Good choice."

1140
01:12:47,397 --> 01:12:48,314
"Good choice."

1141
01:12:48,856 --> 01:12:50,689
"Good choice... Good choice."

1142
01:12:51,638 --> 01:12:54,097
[screaming]
"Yes, he is her husband."

1143
01:12:55,292 --> 01:12:57,501
"Uncle,
I get shocked whenever I touch her."

1144
01:12:58,814 --> 01:13:00,064
"Did you get shocked?"

1145
01:13:00,897 --> 01:13:05,272
"In the movie Magadheera, Ram Charan
gets a shock when Kajal touches him."

1146
01:13:11,606 --> 01:13:12,522
Hey, brother Yadhi.

1147
01:13:12,731 --> 01:13:13,397
What's up?

1148
01:13:13,522 --> 01:13:14,731
You got a new spike hairstyle.

1149
01:13:14,939 --> 01:13:15,897
I heard that you got married.

1150
01:13:16,064 --> 01:13:18,647
Brother,
I heard you broke the cot last night.

1151
01:13:20,022 --> 01:13:20,564
Bye.

1152
01:13:24,522 --> 01:13:25,564
Hey, Yadhi.

1153
01:13:25,981 --> 01:13:27,606
Do you think only you got married?

1154
01:13:28,256 --> 01:13:30,089
Didn't we also get married
and have children?

1155
01:13:30,356 --> 01:13:32,147
I heard you broke the cot last night.

1156
01:13:32,570 --> 01:13:33,612
Hey! Hey! Hey!

1157
01:13:33,814 --> 01:13:34,731
Are you feeling shy?

1158
01:13:36,689 --> 01:13:39,022
It seems Yadigiri's wife
is beautiful than me?

1159
01:13:40,231 --> 01:13:42,981
I heard Yadhi broke the cot last night.

1160
01:13:43,272 --> 01:13:43,772
Yes.

1161
01:13:43,981 --> 01:13:47,106
If I had known earlier that he could
break the cot, I wouldn't have left him.

1162
01:13:47,314 --> 01:13:49,356
- I would have stuck to him.
- Is it?

1163
01:13:50,356 --> 01:13:54,522
My wife spends all her money on shopping.

1164
01:13:55,147 --> 01:13:56,897
She is giving me shocks
one after another.

1165
01:13:57,272 --> 01:13:58,189
Bro!

1166
01:13:59,064 --> 01:14:00,189
Bro, these are not shocks at all.

1167
01:14:00,439 --> 01:14:01,606
Real shocks are something else.

1168
01:14:01,897 --> 01:14:03,439
- You have no idea.
- What is he talking?

1169
01:14:08,814 --> 01:14:13,189
[voice muted]

1170
01:14:14,897 --> 01:14:16,522
Bro, super hairstyle.

1171
01:14:18,856 --> 01:14:19,731
Hey, Yadhi.

1172
01:14:20,022 --> 01:14:21,731
Thunderstorms, lightning, screams!

1173
01:14:22,022 --> 01:14:23,647
Last night,
I got a shock when I touched Damini.

1174
01:14:23,856 --> 01:14:25,647
- Where?
- Whole body.

1175
01:14:25,939 --> 01:14:27,022
You are the reason for that, Uncle.

1176
01:14:27,231 --> 01:14:28,064
What did I do?

1177
01:14:28,689 --> 01:14:29,564
Don't you know?

1178
01:14:31,397 --> 01:14:33,064
- Yours is a bond spanning lifetimes.
- Yes.

1179
01:14:38,856 --> 01:14:40,689
By the way, whom did you plan to meet?

1180
01:14:40,897 --> 01:14:41,731
Who did you marry?

1181
01:14:47,772 --> 01:14:48,772
I'll marry her, uncle.

1182
01:14:51,147 --> 01:14:52,397
Hey, you keep quiet.

1183
01:14:52,606 --> 01:14:54,189
Let's talk to your father-in-law, come.

1184
01:14:54,356 --> 01:14:54,981
- Come.
- How?

1185
01:14:55,189 --> 01:14:55,981
- Come, I will say.
- Where to?

1186
01:14:56,147 --> 01:14:56,772
- Come.
- Hey!

1187
01:14:58,814 --> 01:15:01,189
Brother-in-law? Okay, I will talk to him.

1188
01:15:01,606 --> 01:15:02,314
Who?

1189
01:15:02,814 --> 01:15:03,522
Hey, Yadhi!

1190
01:15:04,147 --> 01:15:05,481
- Won't you listen?
- What?

1191
01:15:05,627 --> 01:15:07,168
- Won't you listen to anyone?
- Me?

1192
01:15:07,856 --> 01:15:09,189
Didn't your father-in-law
say at your wedding...

1193
01:15:11,147 --> 01:15:12,439
that if you touch his daughter,
you'll get shocked?"

1194
01:15:13,814 --> 01:15:16,647
I was trying to tell you
something from past few days.

1195
01:15:17,019 --> 01:15:18,103
Hey, listen.

1196
01:15:18,382 --> 01:15:19,132
You should learn to listen.

1197
01:15:19,384 --> 01:15:22,217
I listened to you, right? Magadheera
movie. Ram Charan. Kajal.

1198
01:15:33,772 --> 01:15:35,022
How's the taste, dear?

1199
01:15:36,147 --> 01:15:37,314
- Mother-in-law!
- Yes?

1200
01:15:37,647 --> 01:15:39,314
I think the salt is slightly less.

1201
01:15:39,655 --> 01:15:41,530
Oh no! I forgot it again.

1202
01:15:41,564 --> 01:15:42,564
I always forget.

1203
01:15:45,022 --> 01:15:46,397
- Mother-in-law!
- Yes?

1204
01:15:46,422 --> 01:15:49,213
Can I ask you something?
You won't take me wrong, will you?

1205
01:15:49,689 --> 01:15:50,731
Ask me, dear.

1206
01:15:51,439 --> 01:15:54,772
Why is everyone
in this house so different?

1207
01:15:55,356 --> 01:15:57,064
No one is talking to each other.

1208
01:15:57,731 --> 01:15:59,481
Everyone looks detached.

1209
01:16:01,356 --> 01:16:02,731
You are like this.

1210
01:16:03,189 --> 01:16:05,106
Father-in-laws are like that.

1211
01:16:06,814 --> 01:16:08,022
Not that, mother-in-law.

1212
01:16:08,226 --> 01:16:10,726
He came alone for the
matchmaking meeting.

1213
01:16:10,921 --> 01:16:14,462
Even for the engagement,
the father-in-law came late.

1214
01:16:15,064 --> 01:16:16,814
That means... That means...

1215
01:16:18,269 --> 01:16:19,519
I understood.

1216
01:16:21,356 --> 01:16:23,564
You don't worry.

1217
01:16:23,761 --> 01:16:27,428
Today, I will make my father-in-law
feed you with his hands.

1218
01:16:32,731 --> 01:16:33,647
Cheers!

1219
01:16:37,147 --> 01:16:38,731
It will look good, mother-in-law.

1220
01:16:38,939 --> 01:16:40,439
- It's very cool.
- So nice.

1221
01:16:42,397 --> 01:16:43,731
- Hey, Lakshmi!
- Yes.

1222
01:16:43,897 --> 01:16:44,772
- For how long?
- Mother-in-law.

1223
01:16:45,064 --> 01:16:46,522
You sit. I will go.

1224
01:16:47,314 --> 01:16:48,356
Stay here.

1225
01:16:52,772 --> 01:16:53,981
- Father-in-law!
- Yes.

1226
01:16:58,272 --> 01:16:59,606
Why did you come, dear?

1227
01:17:01,064 --> 01:17:02,147
It's okay, father-in-law.

1228
01:17:06,064 --> 01:17:06,772
Father-in-law!

1229
01:17:07,481 --> 01:17:10,272
If you don't mind,
can I talk to you for two minutes?

1230
01:17:10,522 --> 01:17:11,439
Tell me, dear.

1231
01:17:14,272 --> 01:17:17,689
If I want to talk to Yadhi,
he is never at home.

1232
01:17:18,564 --> 01:17:21,439
Mr. Sapthagiri always
lives in his own world.

1233
01:17:24,231 --> 01:17:28,064
You two are always busy with this work.

1234
01:17:28,772 --> 01:17:29,731
That is...

1235
01:17:30,314 --> 01:17:32,064
I don't know what to say.

1236
01:17:34,731 --> 01:17:37,314
Because of your quarrels,
everyone here is in trouble.

1237
01:17:38,814 --> 01:17:41,439
No one here believes
that you will change.

1238
01:17:42,231 --> 01:17:42,939
But...

1239
01:17:43,856 --> 01:17:45,147
I have that belief.

1240
01:17:47,231 --> 01:17:48,481
I am not saying this
as your daughter-in-law.

1241
01:17:49,189 --> 01:17:51,147
I am saying this as your daughter.

1242
01:17:52,814 --> 01:17:57,939
If you respect my words, you should
come and eat with everyone today.

1243
01:17:58,147 --> 01:17:58,689
Okay?

1244
01:18:17,356 --> 01:18:22,981
Except for drinking hard,
he never asked me if I had eaten.

1245
01:18:23,564 --> 01:18:25,606
I have no such formalities, sister.

1246
01:18:26,064 --> 01:18:28,856
I get up, eat and sleep.
That's it.

1247
01:18:29,272 --> 01:18:31,397
- What else do we have to do?
- That's it.

1248
01:18:31,897 --> 01:18:33,397
Mother! Aunty!

1249
01:18:33,689 --> 01:18:35,064
- Have you both put henna on your hands?
- Yes.

1250
01:18:35,522 --> 01:18:37,564
- [both]: Is it good?
- Today, I will feed you myself.

1251
01:18:37,731 --> 01:18:38,689
Wow!

1252
01:18:39,522 --> 01:18:41,856
At least let me have this
chance to repay you a little.

1253
01:18:48,731 --> 01:18:49,522
Mother!

1254
01:18:50,481 --> 01:18:52,564
This is your son's bite.

1255
01:18:57,439 --> 01:18:58,397
- Aunty!
- Yes?

1256
01:18:59,064 --> 01:19:02,564
Your son may not feed you,
but Yadhi will.

1257
01:19:05,772 --> 01:19:06,856
Is it spicy?

1258
01:19:07,064 --> 01:19:08,147
- No. It's good.
- It's good.

1259
01:19:11,939 --> 01:19:12,897
- Hey, Yadhi!
- Yes.

1260
01:19:13,064 --> 01:19:15,147
Do you feed just us?
Don't you feed our daughter-in-law?

1261
01:19:18,272 --> 01:19:19,147
Damini!

1262
01:19:19,229 --> 01:19:19,937
Come here.

1263
01:19:20,231 --> 01:19:21,647
Why feed Damini?
Damini didn't apply henna.

1264
01:19:21,856 --> 01:19:22,606
You keep quiet.

1265
01:19:23,189 --> 01:19:25,189
- Come and sit.
- Sit.

1266
01:19:27,189 --> 01:19:27,856
Feed her, man.

1267
01:19:28,814 --> 01:19:30,147
Why should I feed her?
Did she apply henna?

1268
01:19:30,814 --> 01:19:31,647
Feed her.

1269
01:19:32,189 --> 01:19:33,231
- Feed her.
- I mean...

1270
01:19:33,481 --> 01:19:34,481
Feed her, man.

1271
01:19:38,189 --> 01:19:39,606
God! God! God!

1272
01:19:40,064 --> 01:19:42,356
God! God! God!

1273
01:19:44,189 --> 01:19:45,314
Feed her, man.

1274
01:19:49,606 --> 01:19:51,106
See this, mother-in-law.

1275
01:19:51,647 --> 01:19:53,397
Why are you
hesitating so much to feed her?

1276
01:19:53,606 --> 01:19:54,897
Look at that idiot,
how he is feeding his wife.

1277
01:19:55,106 --> 01:19:55,647
<i>Idiot.</i>

1278
01:19:55,981 --> 01:19:57,689
- [in Hindi]: Have it.
- [in Hindi]: I won't eat.

1279
01:19:58,022 --> 01:19:59,314
- Feed her.<i>-[in Hindi]: Have it, dear.</i>

1280
01:19:59,481 --> 01:20:00,772
<i>Feeding her will be the end of me.</i>

1281
01:20:02,147 --> 01:20:02,981
Feed her.

1282
01:20:11,022 --> 01:20:12,064
<i>Why didn't I get a shock?</i>

1283
01:20:13,731 --> 01:20:14,772
<i>Is she the same person?</i>

1284
01:20:15,147 --> 01:20:16,522
Feed her another handful of rice.

1285
01:20:16,731 --> 01:20:18,022
You wait, I am feeding her, right?

1286
01:20:18,231 --> 01:20:19,772
You are struggling too much to feed her.

1287
01:20:24,647 --> 01:20:25,564
That's it.

1288
01:20:25,897 --> 01:20:27,356
Isn't it so cute to see, sister?

1289
01:20:30,772 --> 01:20:32,064
Feed her another handful of rice.

1290
01:20:51,231 --> 01:20:52,606
- Enough...
- Have it, dear.

1291
01:20:52,981 --> 01:20:54,522
Enough, mother-in-law.

1292
01:20:54,648 --> 01:20:56,356
Come on, she is feeling shy.

1293
01:21:00,814 --> 01:21:01,772
Why didn't I get the shock?

1294
01:21:19,939 --> 01:21:21,189
[in Hindi]: Come on, have it.

1295
01:21:21,397 --> 01:21:23,147
- Hey, Yadhi!
- [in Hindi]: Come on, have it.

1296
01:21:23,356 --> 01:21:25,106
Why is he repeatedly saying "cabbage"?

1297
01:21:25,397 --> 01:21:28,147
- [in Hindi]: Come on, have it.
- It's not cabbage.

1298
01:21:28,814 --> 01:21:30,856
It's "khavoji",
which means "please eat."

1299
01:21:31,439 --> 01:21:32,481
[in Hindi]: Please eat.

1300
01:21:39,689 --> 01:21:41,439
<i>That day, I got shocked.</i>

1301
01:21:41,814 --> 01:21:42,939
<i>But I didn't get shocked today.</i>

1302
01:21:44,189 --> 01:21:45,731
<i>Why didn't I get shocked today?</i>

1303
01:21:47,522 --> 01:21:49,106
<i>What's wrong with trying one more time?</i>

1304
01:22:00,397 --> 01:22:01,772
80 acers...

1305
01:22:15,022 --> 01:22:16,106
[electric crackles]

1306
01:22:32,356 --> 01:22:34,106
<i>Why did I get shocked again last night?</i>

1307
01:22:38,481 --> 01:22:39,439
Mom, tea.

1308
01:22:41,856 --> 01:22:42,772
Yadhi.

1309
01:22:43,772 --> 01:22:45,647
Your mother and
father went to the temple.

1310
01:22:47,564 --> 01:22:49,647
Yadhi, why are you running away?

1311
01:22:49,981 --> 01:22:52,606
- Why did you come to me last night?
- When did I come?

1312
01:22:52,856 --> 01:22:53,689
Didn't you come?

1313
01:22:54,314 --> 01:22:55,106
I didn't.

1314
01:22:55,731 --> 01:22:56,606
Is it so?

1315
01:22:56,939 --> 01:22:57,897
It is.

1316
01:22:59,939 --> 01:23:00,689
Look...

1317
01:23:00,939 --> 01:23:03,689
My father tried to tell you many times.

1318
01:23:03,981 --> 01:23:04,731
You didn't listen.

1319
01:23:06,356 --> 01:23:07,647
Hey, I am telling you.

1320
01:23:07,939 --> 01:23:09,064
Hey, Yadhi!

1321
01:23:09,272 --> 01:23:09,856
Stop!

1322
01:23:11,981 --> 01:23:13,397
Yadhi, don't you listen?

1323
01:23:14,022 --> 01:23:14,772
I won't.

1324
01:23:14,981 --> 01:23:17,064
Don't you listen to anyone?

1325
01:23:17,564 --> 01:23:18,439
I won't listen to everyone.

1326
01:23:18,689 --> 01:23:19,606
I won't listen to you at all.

1327
01:23:25,397 --> 01:23:27,439
If you have the guts,
speak to me from there itself.

1328
01:23:28,231 --> 01:23:30,481
Yadhi,
is there electricity in your house?

1329
01:23:30,689 --> 01:23:32,772
Not just power,
there's a transformer here. Come.

1330
01:23:34,731 --> 01:23:35,772
Hey, Yadhi!

1331
01:23:36,272 --> 01:23:37,314
- Amorous play...
- Stop!

1332
01:23:37,939 --> 01:23:39,064
- Stop I say.
- No!

1333
01:23:39,272 --> 01:23:40,314
Just like your grandfather.

1334
01:23:44,314 --> 01:23:46,064
- No, don't come.
- Yadhi, stop!

1335
01:23:46,147 --> 01:23:48,064
They decorated the goddess
so well today, right?

1336
01:23:48,147 --> 01:23:49,397
- Stop...
- I am telling you...

1337
01:23:50,314 --> 01:23:51,147
Oh no!

1338
01:23:53,606 --> 01:23:54,689
Bless me.

1339
01:23:59,147 --> 01:24:00,064
Oopsh!

1340
01:24:05,356 --> 01:24:07,106
They brought up her so well.

1341
01:24:07,356 --> 01:24:08,606
Oh dear!

1342
01:24:11,356 --> 01:24:13,314
Who is taking blessings nowadays, sister?

1343
01:24:15,231 --> 01:24:16,856
Do you want only his blessings?

1344
01:24:17,106 --> 01:24:18,981
Will you take our blessings too?

1345
01:24:19,856 --> 01:24:20,856
Nothing like that, father-in-law.

1346
01:24:21,106 --> 01:24:22,147
I will take your blessings also.

1347
01:24:22,314 --> 01:24:23,272
Give her blessings you'd know.

1348
01:24:29,856 --> 01:24:30,522
Mom!

1349
01:24:30,772 --> 01:24:31,981
Keep Dad's photo ready.

1350
01:24:32,272 --> 01:24:33,356
- Photo?
- What do you mean, man?

1351
01:24:38,064 --> 01:24:40,314
Damini, take my uncle's
blessings instead of my father's.

1352
01:24:40,445 --> 01:24:41,778
Why must she take my blessings?

1353
01:24:42,981 --> 01:24:44,772
I don't have any photo.
Oh no!

1354
01:24:46,064 --> 01:24:48,022
Mom, I have work.
I am going to the party office.

1355
01:24:48,356 --> 01:24:49,314
A second more and I’d be dead.

1356
01:24:49,481 --> 01:24:50,606
I am going inside.

1357
01:24:52,481 --> 01:24:54,189
Either the electricity office
or the party office.

1358
01:24:55,314 --> 01:24:56,481
Don't pay attention to him.

1359
01:24:56,689 --> 01:24:57,772
Today is an auspicious day.

1360
01:24:58,022 --> 01:24:58,814
- Visit the temple.
- Yes.

1361
01:24:59,189 --> 01:25:00,231
Okay, mother-in-law.

1362
01:25:00,439 --> 01:25:02,272
Yadhi, take your wife to the temple.

1363
01:25:03,022 --> 01:25:03,897
Why to the temple?

1364
01:25:04,231 --> 01:25:05,106
Don't say like that.

1365
01:25:05,272 --> 01:25:06,897
After marriage,
you should take your wife along too.

1366
01:25:07,106 --> 01:25:07,856
Yadhi, wait.

1367
01:25:08,481 --> 01:25:09,564
I may die if I take her with me.

1368
01:25:11,397 --> 01:25:12,564
There is no petrol in the bike.

1369
01:25:12,897 --> 01:25:15,064
We will walk. It's also good for health.

1370
01:25:15,897 --> 01:25:17,522
How can you make your wife walk?

1371
01:25:17,689 --> 01:25:19,481
What kind of a person are you?
Take her in the car.

1372
01:25:19,731 --> 01:25:20,856
Where is the car? Uncle has taken it.

1373
01:25:21,064 --> 01:25:21,814
You go and do your work.

1374
01:25:22,231 --> 01:25:23,272
He will say like that, dear.

1375
01:25:23,481 --> 01:25:24,272
You go and get ready.

1376
01:25:28,231 --> 01:25:32,272
[teasing]

1377
01:25:35,689 --> 01:25:36,939
Brother, look over there.

1378
01:25:40,397 --> 01:25:41,564
Who is she?

1379
01:25:41,672 --> 01:25:42,839
She looks new.

1380
01:25:43,272 --> 01:25:44,772
Not that. Look beside her.

1381
01:25:47,814 --> 01:25:48,689
He is our Yadhi?

1382
01:25:48,981 --> 01:25:50,397
Why did he come here?

1383
01:25:50,856 --> 01:25:51,439
Let's go.

1384
01:25:53,356 --> 01:25:54,106
Oh, brother!

1385
01:25:54,397 --> 01:25:57,897
Maybe he came to pray to God to win
the election at least this time, brother.

1386
01:25:58,105 --> 01:26:00,105
Whether he wins or not,

1387
01:26:00,314 --> 01:26:02,564
he promised to repair school,

1388
01:26:02,772 --> 01:26:06,647
build roads, and waive farmer loans.

1389
01:26:06,897 --> 01:26:08,606
We will see what he will do.

1390
01:26:08,814 --> 01:26:10,231
Defeated Sarpanch!

1391
01:26:10,522 --> 01:26:12,064
Hey, naughty boy.

1392
01:26:17,314 --> 01:26:19,564
Hubby, they are mocking you.

1393
01:26:19,856 --> 01:26:20,981
Avoid them. Come.

1394
01:26:26,106 --> 01:26:26,772
God!

1395
01:26:27,897 --> 01:26:30,731
I got so many shocks because I was greedy
for my grandfather's 80 acres of land.

1396
01:26:30,756 --> 01:26:32,064
- Show me the way, God.
- Son,

1397
01:26:32,481 --> 01:26:34,272
you shouldn't pray while
standing directly in front of God.

1398
01:26:35,897 --> 01:26:37,231
Listen to me first.

1399
01:26:38,564 --> 01:26:39,856
He won't listen to anyone.

1400
01:26:40,106 --> 01:26:40,814
Not like that, dear.

1401
01:26:41,272 --> 01:26:43,064
You have to make him listen.

1402
01:26:54,231 --> 01:26:55,689
Make me win at least this time, God.

1403
01:26:55,897 --> 01:26:57,772
If I win, I will shave my head.

1404
01:26:58,522 --> 01:27:01,064
If you lose,
the villagers will shave your head.

1405
01:27:03,856 --> 01:27:05,106
- Let's go.
- [wooing]

1406
01:27:10,106 --> 01:27:11,814
Can you stay here for
a couple of minutes?

1407
01:27:11,892 --> 01:27:13,309
I have to give some offerings.

1408
01:27:13,362 --> 01:27:14,362
I will offer and come.

1409
01:27:39,022 --> 01:27:40,272
[groans in pain]

1410
01:27:46,564 --> 01:27:47,189
Wow!

1411
01:28:07,939 --> 01:28:09,981
[groans in pain]

1412
01:28:39,439 --> 01:28:40,939
Please move. Move!

1413
01:28:43,897 --> 01:28:47,439
[groans in pain]

1414
01:28:54,397 --> 01:28:55,772
Are these the offerings you have given?

1415
01:29:04,856 --> 01:29:05,731
Oopsh!

1416
01:29:13,314 --> 01:29:18,106
"You stay in my eyes all the time."

1417
01:29:19,231 --> 01:29:23,897
"My eyes are filled with your presence."

1418
01:29:24,897 --> 01:29:29,689
"My days are filled with you."

1419
01:29:30,397 --> 01:29:35,439
"I feel lifeless without you."

1420
01:29:36,314 --> 01:29:41,064
"Love, I love you."

1421
01:29:41,731 --> 01:29:46,356
"I am in love with you."

1422
01:29:48,147 --> 01:29:52,481
"If I'm with you,"

1423
01:29:53,147 --> 01:29:57,897
"I feel like I'm with myself."

1424
01:29:59,981 --> 01:30:05,231
"All this mischief
is because of your love."

1425
01:30:05,772 --> 01:30:08,647
"Why this hide-and-seek?"

1426
01:30:08,856 --> 01:30:10,856
Eventually, I'll find
a solution to your problem.

1427
01:30:11,481 --> 01:30:16,647
"Your love engulfed me like a flood."

1428
01:30:17,189 --> 01:30:20,856
"What spell did you cast on me?"

1429
01:30:35,022 --> 01:30:40,856
"Like clouds and the overcast
sky existing in the same place,"

1430
01:30:41,022 --> 01:30:44,606
"we lived separately all these days."

1431
01:30:46,731 --> 01:30:52,522
"The raindrops connected
this distance like a thread."

1432
01:30:52,856 --> 01:30:57,231
"We won't become distant forever."

1433
01:30:57,939 --> 01:31:03,314
"By renewing our love,"

1434
01:31:03,981 --> 01:31:09,314
"infatuation blossomed within us again."

1435
01:31:09,772 --> 01:31:16,981
"As the barriers faded away,
I read your heart."

1436
01:31:31,647 --> 01:31:33,356
Yadhi, stop here.

1437
01:31:34,856 --> 01:31:35,772
How are you?

1438
01:31:36,939 --> 01:31:39,731
- You should study well.
- Okay.

1439
01:31:40,314 --> 01:31:41,064
Let's go.

1440
01:31:48,231 --> 01:31:49,231
I forgot.

1441
01:31:51,439 --> 01:31:52,647
- I am giving.
- Take it.

1442
01:31:53,064 --> 01:31:53,981
Be careful.

1443
01:31:57,106 --> 01:32:01,356
"Love, I love you."

1444
01:32:02,314 --> 01:32:07,147
"I am sharing my love with you."

1445
01:32:08,731 --> 01:32:13,147
"There is no..."

1446
01:32:13,731 --> 01:32:18,856
"...you and me anymore."

1447
01:32:20,522 --> 01:32:25,731
"All this mischief
is because of your love."

1448
01:32:26,439 --> 01:32:28,647
"It feels so good,"

1449
01:32:28,897 --> 01:32:30,647
- I don't come, brother.
- "my dear".

1450
01:32:32,772 --> 01:32:34,189
The dress is amazing.

1451
01:32:34,481 --> 01:32:36,231
Why isn't it amazing
when it costs Rs. 10,000?

1452
01:32:36,689 --> 01:32:37,564
- Rs. 10,000?
- Yes.

1453
01:32:37,772 --> 01:32:39,606
- Where did you get it from?
- I took it from your locker.

1454
01:32:42,272 --> 01:32:43,731
- From my locker?
- Yes.

1455
01:32:43,939 --> 01:32:44,772
Oh, God!

1456
01:33:01,897 --> 01:33:03,439
Yadhi never listens to me.

1457
01:33:03,647 --> 01:33:04,939
- Is it?
- Yes.

1458
01:33:05,231 --> 01:33:06,689
At least you convince him.

1459
01:33:07,481 --> 01:33:08,481
Here, take it.

1460
01:33:09,231 --> 01:33:11,481
What, Yadhi?
Don't you listen to your mother?

1461
01:33:11,689 --> 01:33:13,064
Yes, I don't.

1462
01:33:13,272 --> 01:33:14,106
So what?

1463
01:33:16,356 --> 01:33:17,564
Don't you listen
to her even if I say so?

1464
01:33:18,606 --> 01:33:19,689
No, I don't listen
to her even if you say so.

1465
01:33:19,939 --> 01:33:21,314
- You...
- Oh God!

1466
01:33:23,064 --> 01:33:24,647
- How are you, son-in-law?
- Greetings, father-in-law.

1467
01:33:24,939 --> 01:33:27,356
- Father, is everyone fine in the village?
- Here.

1468
01:33:27,939 --> 01:33:28,939
Everyone is fine.

1469
01:33:29,272 --> 01:33:32,397
But they repeatedly told me
not to bring you there.

1470
01:33:36,522 --> 01:33:37,314
Hey!

1471
01:33:37,772 --> 01:33:40,106
Damini!

1472
01:34:02,397 --> 01:34:03,606
You must vote.

1473
01:34:06,564 --> 01:34:07,231
Greetings.

1474
01:34:07,481 --> 01:34:08,814
Uncle, vote for the bell symbol.

1475
01:34:12,314 --> 01:34:14,689
What is this? Why are the ladies
campaigning instead of Yadhi?

1476
01:34:17,522 --> 01:34:19,647
He said,
"I'll build roads even if I lose," right?

1477
01:34:20,356 --> 01:34:21,564
Where is Yadhi?

1478
01:34:22,147 --> 01:34:24,439
He said he would build roads
even if he don't win.

1479
01:34:24,513 --> 01:34:25,347
He didn't do it.

1480
01:34:25,560 --> 01:34:27,976
But what are you doing after winning?

1481
01:34:30,772 --> 01:34:31,772
Let's go.

1482
01:34:38,731 --> 01:34:39,481
Hey!

1483
01:34:39,981 --> 01:34:42,189
There are a lot of stones in this rice.

1484
01:34:43,314 --> 01:34:44,272
Greetings, brother.

1485
01:34:45,189 --> 01:34:46,647
Hey, you are here.

1486
01:34:46,856 --> 01:34:47,939
What is happening in the village?

1487
01:34:49,314 --> 01:34:53,106
The whole village is talking
about my brother winning, brother.

1488
01:34:53,397 --> 01:34:55,356
You should celebrate the baby shower.

1489
01:34:55,814 --> 01:34:57,814
Then you will be the talk of the town.

1490
01:34:59,356 --> 01:35:03,522
- That is...
- I got it.

1491
01:35:03,939 --> 01:35:04,772
Give me the money.

1492
01:35:07,606 --> 01:35:09,897
What about that?
Will you keep it inside? Take it out.

1493
01:35:10,147 --> 01:35:11,147
He is my brother.

1494
01:35:13,939 --> 01:35:14,939
Celebrate the function.

1495
01:35:15,606 --> 01:35:16,231
Carry on.

1496
01:35:16,522 --> 01:35:20,189
Brother,
I will get those 80 acres, right?

1497
01:35:21,647 --> 01:35:22,772
You will.

1498
01:35:23,272 --> 01:35:25,939
So, should I run for ward member
in the next election?

1499
01:35:26,314 --> 01:35:28,272
You are my brother.

1500
01:35:29,522 --> 01:35:30,314
I am here.

1501
01:35:30,522 --> 01:35:31,314
- Go.
- Thanks, brother.

1502
01:35:31,606 --> 01:35:33,147
- Bye. Well done.
- Bye.

1503
01:35:33,397 --> 01:35:34,439
See you in the function, brother.

1504
01:35:35,481 --> 01:35:38,647
Brother,
he wants the ward member post now.

1505
01:35:39,356 --> 01:35:41,022
Maybe next he'll ask
to become the village head.

1506
01:35:41,939 --> 01:35:44,147
Brother, he seems suspicious

1507
01:35:45,731 --> 01:35:48,106
You don't worry, I will take care.

1508
01:35:48,981 --> 01:35:50,314
HAPPY HOME

1509
01:35:52,814 --> 01:35:53,606
Greetings, uncle.

1510
01:35:55,689 --> 01:35:57,397
- Greetings, brother.
- Hey, how are you?

1511
01:35:57,606 --> 01:35:58,356
I am good.

1512
01:35:58,689 --> 01:35:59,522
Please come, brother.

1513
01:36:04,147 --> 01:36:04,689
- Come.
- Greetings.

1514
01:36:04,897 --> 01:36:05,606
Greetings.

1515
01:36:06,147 --> 01:36:07,356
Greetings. Come.

1516
01:36:07,939 --> 01:36:09,314
- Greetings.
- Greetings.

1517
01:36:10,981 --> 01:36:13,731
- May you get married soon.
- Brother, this is baby shower ceremony.

1518
01:36:14,689 --> 01:36:16,314
Take a good picture.

1519
01:36:22,689 --> 01:36:23,481
Come, come.

1520
01:36:23,897 --> 01:36:24,939
They are our daughter-in-law's relatives.

1521
01:36:25,106 --> 01:36:26,272
- [in Rajasthani]: Greetings.
- Greetings.

1522
01:36:26,522 --> 01:36:27,522
[in Rajasthani]: Have a healthy baby.

1523
01:36:27,731 --> 01:36:28,689
- Greetings.
- [in Rajasthani]: Greetings.

1524
01:36:28,981 --> 01:36:29,689
[in Rajasthani]: Greetings.

1525
01:36:30,022 --> 01:36:31,314
- [in Rajasthani]: Greetings.
- Greetings.

1526
01:36:31,522 --> 01:36:32,731
[in Rajasthani]: Have a healthy baby.

1527
01:36:34,106 --> 01:36:34,689
[in Rajasthani]: Greetings.

1528
01:36:35,272 --> 01:36:36,689
Son, why are you late?

1529
01:36:36,939 --> 01:36:38,231
The way is a little confusing.

1530
01:36:38,439 --> 01:36:39,897
Is it? At least you came on time.

1531
01:36:40,147 --> 01:36:41,356
[indistinct voices]

1532
01:36:42,522 --> 01:36:43,772
[in Hindi]: How are you, my dear?

1533
01:36:49,939 --> 01:36:51,397
Hey, what is this?

1534
01:36:52,188 --> 01:36:53,956
- [in Hindi]: Who is he?
- Why is he hugging your wife?

1535
01:36:53,981 --> 01:36:55,689
It's okay, mother.
It's brother-sister relationship.

1536
01:36:55,897 --> 01:36:56,481
You wait, man.

1537
01:36:56,689 --> 01:36:57,647
Sit down.

1538
01:36:57,856 --> 01:36:59,397
Being his
brother-in-law, are you coming now?

1539
01:36:59,647 --> 01:37:01,106
Don't you know that you should
help your brother-in-law?

1540
01:37:01,314 --> 01:37:02,231
[In Hindi]: What is she saying?

1541
01:37:02,606 --> 01:37:03,647
Mother, wait.

1542
01:37:03,897 --> 01:37:06,147
- Brother-in-law, you come.
- What did I say now?

1543
01:37:06,314 --> 01:37:07,481
- What is he doing?
- Come, man.

1544
01:37:07,689 --> 01:37:10,147
Hey, listen to me.

1545
01:37:10,172 --> 01:37:12,589
- [in Hindi]: Where are you taking me?
- Don't shout. Listen to me.

1546
01:37:12,614 --> 01:37:13,197
Hey, shut up.

1547
01:37:13,772 --> 01:37:14,981
Why didn't you answer the phone?

1548
01:37:15,147 --> 01:37:15,856
Pay the rent.

1549
01:37:16,022 --> 01:37:16,731
Hey, don't shout.

1550
01:37:16,939 --> 01:37:18,064
- It's just three months.
- Listen to me...

1551
01:37:18,272 --> 01:37:18,772
Pay the money.

1552
01:37:18,981 --> 01:37:20,314
- After that, do whatever you want.
- <i>Who is this guy?</i>

1553
01:37:20,606 --> 01:37:22,439
Hey, brother.
I will pay you, brother.

1554
01:37:22,731 --> 01:37:24,314
Give me some time, brother.

1555
01:37:24,689 --> 01:37:26,397
- Pay the money first.
- Quiet, brother-in-law.

1556
01:37:28,356 --> 01:37:30,231
Pay the money first.
Do whatever you want later.

1557
01:37:30,606 --> 01:37:32,231
Oh God, he gets
into arguments with him too.

1558
01:37:32,772 --> 01:37:34,439
I told you, right?
This is the right time.

1559
01:37:39,064 --> 01:37:39,772
Madam!

1560
01:37:41,272 --> 01:37:44,356
The girl sitting in that chair
is not your son's wife.

1561
01:37:44,897 --> 01:37:45,397
Hey.

1562
01:37:46,272 --> 01:37:47,814
What is this? What is he saying?

1563
01:37:48,022 --> 01:37:49,647
I might get a heart attack. Come here.

1564
01:37:51,022 --> 01:37:52,439
Brother, what are you talking?

1565
01:37:52,939 --> 01:37:54,689
- It's nothing, mother.
- No... No.

1566
01:37:55,356 --> 01:37:57,314
- A wife is a duty, mother.
- [in Hindi]: Go away from here.

1567
01:37:58,064 --> 01:38:00,231
Listen to me. Please, brother.

1568
01:38:00,522 --> 01:38:02,689
Brother... I will pay up.

1569
01:38:02,939 --> 01:38:04,731
It's not that, brother.

1570
01:38:04,939 --> 01:38:05,897
Nothing like that, Mother.

1571
01:38:06,106 --> 01:38:07,814
- I will talk to him.
- Look at them both.

1572
01:38:08,606 --> 01:38:09,606
They are husband and wife.

1573
01:38:09,939 --> 01:38:11,022
They are not brother and sister.

1574
01:38:11,356 --> 01:38:13,106
- Oh no!
- Let's talk outside, brother.

1575
01:38:13,689 --> 01:38:15,564
- Please don't create a scene, brother.
- What is this? What is he saying?

1576
01:38:15,814 --> 01:38:17,272
Your son didn't pay the rent.

1577
01:38:17,481 --> 01:38:18,481
Oh no!

1578
01:38:18,856 --> 01:38:20,814
- He came here to take his wife.
- Let's go out and talk, brother.

1579
01:38:21,106 --> 01:38:21,981
- What is he saying?
- Listen...

1580
01:38:22,189 --> 01:38:23,731
How can you rent out another man's wife?

1581
01:38:24,522 --> 01:38:26,606
You have insulted the village.
You cheap fellow.

1582
01:38:26,856 --> 01:38:27,772
What is this, Sapthagiri?

1583
01:38:27,981 --> 01:38:29,606
Will you do anything
for 80 acres of land?

1584
01:38:30,064 --> 01:38:31,022
Is it ethical?

1585
01:38:31,189 --> 01:38:32,897
I imagined something
like this would happen.

1586
01:38:33,314 --> 01:38:34,314
- What is this?
- That is...

1587
01:38:34,522 --> 01:38:35,189
[indistinct voices]

1588
01:38:35,397 --> 01:38:36,397
- What is this nuisance?
- Listen to me, father.

1589
01:38:36,606 --> 01:38:37,606
- I am dealing, dad.
- What is this?

1590
01:38:37,814 --> 01:38:38,606
What can you handle?

1591
01:38:39,064 --> 01:38:40,231
- You did all the wrong things.
- Pay me money first,

1592
01:38:40,439 --> 01:38:42,272
- After that, do what you want.
- How can you rent your wife.

1593
01:38:42,481 --> 01:38:43,397
You are such an idiot.

1594
01:38:43,606 --> 01:38:44,314
Beat him.

1595
01:38:44,564 --> 01:38:47,939
[indistinct voices]

1596
01:38:48,147 --> 01:38:49,106
How dare you hit my father?

1597
01:38:56,397 --> 01:38:57,147
- Hey!
- What are you thinking of yourself?

1598
01:38:57,356 --> 01:38:58,314
- Leave me.
- Stop them, uncle.

1599
01:38:58,522 --> 01:39:00,731
- Oh no! Stop them.
- Why are you beating me?

1600
01:39:01,439 --> 01:39:03,064
Hold him like that.

1601
01:39:03,731 --> 01:39:06,564
[indistinct voices]

1602
01:39:07,439 --> 01:39:08,981
You came to my house and fight here?

1603
01:39:09,189 --> 01:39:10,189
- Listen to me.
- Get out.

1604
01:39:11,231 --> 01:39:12,939
Who are they? What is this nonsense?

1605
01:39:16,981 --> 01:39:17,814
Yadhi.

1606
01:39:25,647 --> 01:39:26,731
Oh no!

1607
01:39:31,564 --> 01:39:33,689
Huh! Did you see that?

1608
01:39:35,522 --> 01:39:37,022
That's why the cot was broken.

1609
01:39:48,106 --> 01:39:49,647
[voice muted]

1610
01:39:53,439 --> 01:39:55,147
Yadhi is not innocent.

1611
01:39:55,772 --> 01:39:59,147
He married her to get 80 acres of land.

1612
01:40:01,022 --> 01:40:03,064
He even took Rs. 25 lakhs as dowry.

1613
01:40:07,689 --> 01:40:11,314
Everyone's life will be at danger
if we keep such a woman in our village.

1614
01:40:16,522 --> 01:40:17,397
This is our family issue.

1615
01:40:17,939 --> 01:40:18,939
Please leave.

1616
01:40:26,189 --> 01:40:26,856
Let's go.

1617
01:40:27,064 --> 01:40:28,106
Our work is done.

1618
01:40:40,356 --> 01:40:41,439
Sorry, dear.

1619
01:40:42,022 --> 01:40:43,481
It happened unknowingly.

1620
01:40:43,731 --> 01:40:45,397
Shh! Keep quiet.

1621
01:40:48,939 --> 01:40:49,814
Why should I be quiet?

1622
01:40:50,397 --> 01:40:52,522
You married me for 80 acres of property.

1623
01:40:54,772 --> 01:40:57,189
So you didn't marry me
because you loved me?

1624
01:40:58,106 --> 01:41:00,106
Damini, we will talk later.

1625
01:41:01,481 --> 01:41:03,689
You married me for a baby boy.

1626
01:41:04,106 --> 01:41:04,772
Isn't it?

1627
01:41:05,022 --> 01:41:05,731
Isn't it?

1628
01:41:07,231 --> 01:41:08,606
I planned to tell you at the right time.

1629
01:41:08,772 --> 01:41:12,106
Because you hid all of this, you ended up
with a wife who gives you shocks!

1630
01:41:12,564 --> 01:41:13,397
What are you talking?

1631
01:41:18,314 --> 01:41:20,772
Did you take the dowry?

1632
01:41:22,481 --> 01:41:23,356
Tell me.

1633
01:41:23,689 --> 01:41:24,981
I had to take it to put up with you.

1634
01:41:29,397 --> 01:41:32,522
I looked for love in you
after my parents and my friend Malli.

1635
01:41:35,772 --> 01:41:39,189
But I found only selfishness in you,
not love.

1636
01:41:40,022 --> 01:41:41,356
But I married you out of love.

1637
01:41:42,272 --> 01:41:43,064
Out of love?

1638
01:41:44,731 --> 01:41:45,939
You didn't marry me out of love.

1639
01:41:46,147 --> 01:41:47,897
You married me by hiding everything.

1640
01:41:49,397 --> 01:41:50,397
Oh! That's why.

1641
01:41:50,689 --> 01:41:53,272
You told me to meditate
and control my heart beat.

1642
01:41:53,439 --> 01:41:54,856
I thought it was love.

1643
01:41:55,939 --> 01:41:57,981
Your plan was to get married,
have a baby boy, and get the property.

1644
01:41:58,231 --> 01:41:58,814
Isn't it?

1645
01:41:59,064 --> 01:42:00,314
- Tell me.
- Yes.

1646
01:42:00,647 --> 01:42:02,106
I married you for the property.

1647
01:42:02,314 --> 01:42:03,022
What is it now?

1648
01:42:04,856 --> 01:42:05,606
Hey!

1649
01:42:05,939 --> 01:42:07,272
Anyway, who would even marry you?

1650
01:42:07,814 --> 01:42:11,231
Your father and your whole village
dumped you on me and cut my throat!

1651
01:42:13,022 --> 01:42:15,356
Stay if you want.
Otherwise, leave.

1652
01:42:15,522 --> 01:42:16,397
[both]: Yadhi!

1653
01:42:17,856 --> 01:42:20,064
It doesn't matter if you stay or not.

1654
01:42:21,272 --> 01:42:22,231
If not you, I'll find another girl.

1655
01:42:27,481 --> 01:42:29,856
- Is it?
- It is.

1656
01:42:34,397 --> 01:42:35,439
Dear, Damini.

1657
01:42:37,022 --> 01:42:37,772
Mother!

1658
01:42:38,897 --> 01:42:40,689
She is leaving. Stop her, son.

1659
01:42:41,147 --> 01:42:42,189
Just let her go.

1660
01:42:43,731 --> 01:42:45,606
- She is leaving. Stop her, son.
- Mother.

1661
01:42:47,481 --> 01:42:48,397
Damini.

1662
01:42:48,647 --> 01:42:51,481
They suddenly invited for the function
and I got late due to bus delay.

1663
01:42:56,356 --> 01:42:57,772
Damini, where are you going?

1664
01:42:57,981 --> 01:42:58,897
What happened?

1665
01:43:03,356 --> 01:43:04,272
Son-in-law!

1666
01:43:17,439 --> 01:43:19,439
Brother, where is your wife?

1667
01:43:22,689 --> 01:43:23,356
Oopsh!

1668
01:43:27,397 --> 01:43:29,522
"Suddenly,
someone's jealousy may have affected you."

1669
01:43:29,606 --> 01:43:31,606
"Someone may cast an evil eye."

1670
01:43:32,189 --> 01:43:36,314
"This story turned upside down."

1671
01:43:36,897 --> 01:43:39,022
"There is no right or wrong."

1672
01:43:39,314 --> 01:43:41,731
- "Where is the way to appease?"
- Son, are you obeying?

1673
01:43:42,022 --> 01:43:43,856
- "This truth has no answer."
- Where is your wife?

1674
01:43:46,564 --> 01:43:48,606
"These hearts are..."

1675
01:43:50,397 --> 01:43:54,814
"...broken into halves."

1676
01:43:55,772 --> 01:44:00,231
"The dreams remained just dreams."

1677
01:44:00,564 --> 01:44:04,981
"This is the moment of tears."

1678
01:44:05,772 --> 01:44:09,231
"These hearts are..."

1679
01:44:09,856 --> 01:44:14,106
"...broken into halves."

1680
01:44:23,772 --> 01:44:25,106
Not his throat...

1681
01:44:25,564 --> 01:44:28,356
If you have guts,
go and choke your wife's throat.

1682
01:44:29,897 --> 01:44:31,147
He can't.

1683
01:44:42,814 --> 01:44:45,106
Though Malli's husband
has a bad temper,

1684
01:44:45,209 --> 01:44:47,792
he'll look for her and take
her back before sunset.

1685
01:44:48,356 --> 01:44:49,856
- Okay?
- Yes.

1686
01:44:53,272 --> 01:44:55,814
The way you are waiting for Yadhi,

1687
01:44:56,064 --> 01:44:58,606
may be he is waiting for you
in the same way.

1688
01:45:03,814 --> 01:45:09,731
"When the body and soul are separated,"

1689
01:45:09,981 --> 01:45:12,231
"it hurts deeply."

1690
01:45:12,939 --> 01:45:16,897
- "Patching a broken heart is..."
- Dear!

1691
01:45:17,897 --> 01:45:20,106
- Your eyes clearly show your husband.
- "...not so easy."

1692
01:45:21,106 --> 01:45:25,106
To save relationships, sometimes
we have to tolerate hurtful words.

1693
01:45:27,689 --> 01:45:33,106
Yadhi, your grandfather used
to scold your grandmother.

1694
01:45:33,314 --> 01:45:36,731
But he never asked her
to leave the house.

1695
01:45:37,314 --> 01:45:40,481
You clearly didn't get
your grandfather's genes for this one.

1696
01:45:49,814 --> 01:45:50,856
What happened, son?

1697
01:45:50,981 --> 01:45:53,814
Uncle, I don't want any property.

1698
01:45:55,189 --> 01:45:56,772
I just want Damini, Uncle.

1699
01:46:16,732 --> 01:46:19,357
- This is yours.
- Tell me, son-in-law what's the matter?

1700
01:46:20,189 --> 01:46:21,397
Cheers.

1701
01:46:21,814 --> 01:46:22,856
Father-in-law!

1702
01:46:24,772 --> 01:46:26,522
I said something because I was angry.

1703
01:46:27,522 --> 01:46:29,522
How could she leave just for that?
You tell me.

1704
01:46:32,231 --> 01:46:34,397
Only if there is anger,
there will be love, right?

1705
01:46:36,397 --> 01:46:37,981
Even in love, there will be anger.

1706
01:46:39,689 --> 01:46:41,689
When I came to your village
for the first time,

1707
01:46:42,439 --> 01:46:45,147
I fell in love with Damini,
father-in-law.

1708
01:46:48,522 --> 01:46:49,647
It's true, father-in-law. Believe me.

1709
01:46:50,731 --> 01:46:52,564
Oh no! All the liquor
has spilled, father-in-law.

1710
01:46:54,939 --> 01:46:56,106
At least this much is left.

1711
01:46:56,522 --> 01:46:57,481
Father-in-law!

1712
01:46:58,939 --> 01:47:00,147
Is it all gone?

1713
01:47:02,856 --> 01:47:04,647
How did you give birth
to this electric shock?

1714
01:47:06,272 --> 01:47:07,606
What do you mean, son-in-law?

1715
01:47:08,231 --> 01:47:09,564
Am I a scientist?

1716
01:47:10,272 --> 01:47:12,064
I am like everyone else.

1717
01:47:12,981 --> 01:47:15,356
Then why does Damini
have this shock power?

1718
01:47:17,814 --> 01:47:18,897
I'll tell you, son-in-law.

1719
01:47:19,064 --> 01:47:21,064
That day, when we were
returning from the festival...

1720
01:47:25,897 --> 01:47:28,481
It's paining, hubby.
I can't bear it, please stop.

1721
01:47:29,439 --> 01:47:30,981
Durga, careful.

1722
01:47:34,814 --> 01:47:37,814
- Come here, come.
- I can't, hubby.

1723
01:47:39,772 --> 01:47:41,106
Sit down.

1724
01:47:41,397 --> 01:47:42,522
Sit down carefully.

1725
01:47:55,022 --> 01:47:55,981
Madam.

1726
01:48:01,897 --> 01:48:05,397
[voice muted]

1727
01:48:09,272 --> 01:48:10,731
Why did you leave her there?

1728
01:48:10,939 --> 01:48:13,314
- Why, madam?
- That's not a good tree.

1729
01:48:36,731 --> 01:48:38,856
Your baby was born with a rare condition.

1730
01:48:39,939 --> 01:48:43,981
When we touch her, we feel a shock
at times and at other times we don't.

1731
01:48:44,981 --> 01:48:47,939
We have no idea when or how that happens.

1732
01:48:48,647 --> 01:48:51,356
As per what you are saying,

1733
01:48:51,381 --> 01:48:54,173
it may be because of the thunder fell on
the tree when her mother was under it.

1734
01:48:54,202 --> 01:48:55,869
Please take good care of your baby.

1735
01:49:01,564 --> 01:49:03,356
Durga, don't.

1736
01:49:14,606 --> 01:49:19,856
♪ Little girl, ♪
♪ your arrival is a miracle. ♪

1737
01:49:20,022 --> 01:49:25,314
♪ Darling girl, ♪
♪ I dedicate my love to you. ♪

1738
01:49:25,856 --> 01:49:30,189
♪ I'm always with you. ♪

1739
01:49:31,356 --> 01:49:35,814
♪ Oh lightning star! ♪
♪ [baby crying] ♪

1740
01:49:35,939 --> 01:49:41,397
♪ I've given birth to you heartfully. ♪

1741
01:49:41,981 --> 01:49:46,564
♪ Oh lightning star! ♪

1742
01:49:47,314 --> 01:49:54,272
[vocalizing]
[baby crying]

1743
01:49:54,689 --> 01:49:59,189
[vocalizing]
[baby crying]

1744
01:49:59,647 --> 01:50:05,147
[baby crying]
♪ A bond established with you. ♪

1745
01:50:05,397 --> 01:50:10,814
♪ Unlimited happiness is ours. ♪

1746
01:50:11,314 --> 01:50:17,147
[children singing birthday song]
♪ You are like this! ♪

1747
01:50:17,314 --> 01:50:20,522
♪ Oh lightning star! ♪
[children singing birthday song]

1748
01:50:20,689 --> 01:50:24,981
♪ I've given birth to you heartfully. ♪
[children singing birthday song]

1749
01:50:26,439 --> 01:50:30,606
<i>I don't know what happened to my Durga,
who survived the thunderbolt that day.</i>

1750
01:50:31,064 --> 01:50:34,481
<i>Maybe God became envious
after seeing our happy family.</i>

1751
01:50:35,231 --> 01:50:37,314
<i>God took Durga away from us.</i>

1752
01:50:37,731 --> 01:50:40,106
<i>The problem that was
cured by Durga's touch...</i>

1753
01:50:40,481 --> 01:50:43,897
<i>...came back to Damini
after Durga's death.</i>

1754
01:50:47,606 --> 01:50:49,272
That means there was no shock in
those ten years, father-in-law?

1755
01:50:50,772 --> 01:50:51,897
It didn't, son-in-law.

1756
01:50:52,314 --> 01:50:53,981
On the following day...

1757
01:50:54,439 --> 01:50:55,231
Dad...

1758
01:50:59,897 --> 01:51:02,397
<i>We who knows only the name Bali Nayak,</i>

1759
01:51:02,981 --> 01:51:04,314
<i>we saw him for the first time.</i>

1760
01:51:04,981 --> 01:51:07,814
<i>He doesn't have the pity
and compassion on kids.</i>

1761
01:51:08,272 --> 01:51:11,814
<i>Any child he sets his eyes on in the
village ends up getting kidnapped</i>

1762
01:51:12,397 --> 01:51:15,397
<i>The stare he gave to
Damini while leaving.</i>

1763
01:51:15,606 --> 01:51:17,106
<i>Started a fear in me.</i>

1764
01:51:18,897 --> 01:51:21,606
A good thing happened to the village
because of her.

1765
01:51:23,106 --> 01:51:24,231
But my daughter...

1766
01:51:25,939 --> 01:51:28,814
I never thought she would be alone.

1767
01:51:29,481 --> 01:51:30,647
Father-in-law, don't cry.

1768
01:51:31,314 --> 01:51:32,314
I am here for you.

1769
01:51:33,314 --> 01:51:34,314
Don't cry.

1770
01:51:35,606 --> 01:51:37,397
Did Damini save so many people,
father-in-law?

1771
01:51:39,814 --> 01:51:43,064
Really, Damini is a super woman.

1772
01:51:45,147 --> 01:51:48,022
I am a useless fellow.

1773
01:51:48,981 --> 01:51:51,231
Do something and bring us together.

1774
01:51:51,481 --> 01:51:52,397
I will bow at your feet.

1775
01:51:53,064 --> 01:51:54,397
Are you listening, father-in-law...?

1776
01:51:56,272 --> 01:51:58,314
It would be good if
that thunder had fell on you.

1777
01:51:58,897 --> 01:52:00,564
I wouldn't have these problems.

1778
01:52:06,522 --> 01:52:08,689
What a plan our boss Narasimha made.

1779
01:52:08,772 --> 01:52:11,522
He entangled both the brothers.

1780
01:52:12,481 --> 01:52:14,106
- You said it well.
- Hey, hmm.

1781
01:52:14,897 --> 01:52:17,189
- Hey, get up.
- Those brothers are finished.

1782
01:52:17,397 --> 01:52:19,647
[in Kannada]: The head of the
village is ours this time.

1783
01:52:21,422 --> 01:52:23,088
Long live Narasimha.

1784
01:52:26,606 --> 01:52:27,314
Drink.

1785
01:52:27,939 --> 01:52:30,189
Those two are useless, brother.

1786
01:52:30,356 --> 01:52:33,856
Our boss Narasimha is so... so happy.

1787
01:52:34,064 --> 01:52:35,731
- Long live Narasimha.
- You said it well.

1788
01:52:48,856 --> 01:52:50,564
What is this, brother?

1789
01:52:51,147 --> 01:52:53,856
I lent Rajasthani wife
because you told me to, right?

1790
01:52:54,647 --> 01:52:57,439
I had a doubt when the ruckus
happened at the function.

1791
01:52:59,231 --> 01:53:00,189
What happened, man?

1792
01:53:00,397 --> 01:53:02,106
Why are you getting worried? Sit.

1793
01:53:02,897 --> 01:53:05,231
Wow! You're acting so well, brother.

1794
01:53:05,647 --> 01:53:07,231
You created problems between us so well.

1795
01:53:09,205 --> 01:53:10,872
Sit down first, man.

1796
01:53:10,897 --> 01:53:11,981
Eat something.

1797
01:53:13,539 --> 01:53:15,539
Drink this. Sit!

1798
01:53:15,748 --> 01:53:17,248
You idiot.

1799
01:53:17,549 --> 01:53:19,674
My brother,
who lost after contesting honestly,

1800
01:53:19,981 --> 01:53:22,272
is greater than people like you
who use cheap tricks to win.

1801
01:53:34,076 --> 01:53:35,076
Yes, Aunt.

1802
01:53:35,503 --> 01:53:38,419
Yadhi, your brother hasn't
come home since yesterday.

1803
01:53:40,647 --> 01:53:42,189
I'm scared of what might have happened.

1804
01:54:38,481 --> 01:54:40,064
Hey, he is your elder brother.

1805
01:54:40,272 --> 01:54:42,147
He will be with you
through good and bad times.

1806
01:56:15,106 --> 01:56:16,647
How dare you mess with Narala family.

1807
01:56:17,647 --> 01:56:18,754
I will pull your nerves out.

1808
01:56:21,314 --> 01:56:22,147
Where is my shirt?

1809
01:56:22,356 --> 01:56:23,189
It' gone.

1810
01:56:23,397 --> 01:56:24,606
You tore it yourself there.

1811
01:56:25,772 --> 01:56:27,814
Hey, see my body.

1812
01:56:32,189 --> 01:56:33,856
The village head's mill may get looted.

1813
01:56:34,231 --> 01:56:35,814
His legs and hands may be broken.

1814
01:56:36,606 --> 01:56:38,064
The crows might peck his bald head.

1815
01:56:39,439 --> 01:56:41,022
Look how he beat him.

1816
01:56:42,647 --> 01:56:44,939
We must kill that village head.

1817
01:56:46,397 --> 01:56:49,606
Uncle, don't feel bad as I'm saying this.

1818
01:56:51,731 --> 01:56:54,856
You are the reason why he is like this.

1819
01:56:57,314 --> 01:56:58,231
Who is he hanging out with?

1820
01:56:58,522 --> 01:57:00,439
What is he doing?
Have you ever cared?

1821
01:57:00,856 --> 01:57:03,564
By associating with that village head,
he has ruined our family's reputation.

1822
01:57:05,481 --> 01:57:07,939
You're not in control,
so how can you control him?

1823
01:57:10,356 --> 01:57:12,106
It's not about what Grandpa gave us.

1824
01:57:12,647 --> 01:57:14,731
What did we achieve?

1825
01:57:17,272 --> 01:57:17,897
Yadhi!

1826
01:57:19,647 --> 01:57:21,647
You are talking so much for your brother.

1827
01:57:22,439 --> 01:57:25,064
But why aren't you
talking about your wife?

1828
01:57:26,814 --> 01:57:29,856
A girl should stay in her mother-in-law's
house after marriage.

1829
01:57:30,397 --> 01:57:31,731
But she shouldn't stay in her mother's
house.

1830
01:57:33,522 --> 01:57:35,731
You are thinking about her problem.

1831
01:57:36,314 --> 01:57:41,314
But did you think about the change
in this house because of her arrival?

1832
01:57:43,231 --> 01:57:45,481
You got married with your selfishness.

1833
01:57:47,147 --> 01:57:50,064
But do you know why
she came to this house?

1834
01:57:50,272 --> 01:57:53,564
She came here to get the
family she doesn't have.

1835
01:57:57,606 --> 01:58:01,314
Damini was the first person who wanted to
change all of us.

1836
01:58:04,856 --> 01:58:06,356
You both don't become like your fathers.

1837
01:58:10,231 --> 01:58:13,814
You don't understand our feelings at
home, so how will you ask for votes?

1838
01:58:14,564 --> 01:58:15,689
How can you serve the village?

1839
01:58:19,356 --> 01:58:21,731
What did innocent Damini do?

1840
01:58:23,939 --> 01:58:25,022
I'm telling you as your mother.

1841
01:58:26,981 --> 01:58:28,564
Go and bring Damini.

1842
01:58:31,272 --> 01:58:31,939
Go.

1843
01:58:36,981 --> 01:58:38,147
Okay, mother.

1844
01:58:40,397 --> 01:58:41,397
Yadhi...

1845
01:58:43,647 --> 01:58:46,731
I'm feeling a strange happiness in me.

1846
01:58:49,439 --> 01:58:52,772
You've obeyed me for the first time, son.

1847
01:59:15,147 --> 01:59:16,231
Don't cry.

1848
01:59:16,564 --> 01:59:17,647
Don't be sad, mom.

1849
01:59:17,981 --> 01:59:19,731
You like our car, don't you?

1850
01:59:20,231 --> 01:59:22,897
Mom,
let's go and bring Damini in our car.

1851
01:59:24,522 --> 01:59:25,606
Yadhi...

1852
01:59:38,397 --> 01:59:41,272
Brother... Start the car.
Let's bring back my daughter-in-law.

1853
01:59:41,689 --> 01:59:43,064
Alright, brother. As you say.

1854
01:59:43,314 --> 01:59:44,356
Come on.

1855
01:59:49,772 --> 01:59:51,106
Have patience. Bear it for a while.

1856
01:59:52,731 --> 01:59:54,314
Keep breathing.

1857
01:59:56,147 --> 01:59:57,314
Bear it.

1858
02:00:01,022 --> 02:00:04,022
It's almost over, dear. Almost done.

1859
02:00:18,814 --> 02:00:22,397
[lady sobbing]

1860
02:00:23,689 --> 02:00:25,772
Why did this happen?

1861
02:00:26,189 --> 02:00:28,439
- Why did this have to happen?
- What happened, old woman?

1862
02:00:29,939 --> 02:00:32,397
The child is born dead.

1863
02:00:35,522 --> 02:00:38,272
God did an injustice to our Malli.

1864
02:00:40,606 --> 02:00:42,356
What wrong did we do?

1865
02:00:43,397 --> 02:00:44,856
[sobbing]

1866
02:00:45,272 --> 02:00:46,897
She can't speak.

1867
02:00:47,147 --> 02:00:49,481
How will my child bear this tragedy?

1868
02:00:52,139 --> 02:00:53,264
Will you also eat some ice cream?

1869
02:00:53,816 --> 02:00:57,358
No, once you're born,
we three shall savour it.

1870
02:01:00,584 --> 02:01:02,459
We visited so many temples.

1871
02:01:03,647 --> 02:01:06,522
But God didn't have mercy on us.

1872
02:01:07,356 --> 02:01:09,981
What did we do to
deserve this curse, dear?

1873
02:01:12,522 --> 02:01:15,981
[infant crying]

1874
02:01:17,147 --> 02:01:17,981
The child is alive.

1875
02:01:29,647 --> 02:01:30,481
Did you all see that?

1876
02:01:30,897 --> 02:01:32,606
Damini saved my child.

1877
02:01:45,064 --> 02:01:46,897
We mistaken you these many days, dear.

1878
02:01:47,231 --> 02:01:48,147
Don't keep it in mind.

1879
02:01:50,272 --> 02:01:51,106
Sorry, sister...

1880
02:01:51,314 --> 02:01:52,772
It's my mistake too.

1881
02:01:52,981 --> 02:01:55,231
I will tell my father
and get you a new TV.

1882
02:01:57,272 --> 02:01:59,856
That day, I told her
spoil the match-making ceremony.

1883
02:02:00,064 --> 02:02:02,856
Because I messed up the
match-making ritual that day...

1884
02:02:03,064 --> 02:02:04,856
Today I bagged a good rank in the Civils.

1885
02:02:05,147 --> 02:02:06,022
Sorry, dear.

1886
02:02:06,356 --> 02:02:08,022
Oh, that's okay.

1887
02:02:09,356 --> 02:02:10,356
Hey, girl.

1888
02:02:11,606 --> 02:02:12,647
Hey, old lady.

1889
02:02:13,064 --> 02:02:16,064
There is no one to make
fun of me or to care for me.

1890
02:02:16,462 --> 02:02:17,670
I thought you were my everything.

1891
02:02:18,104 --> 02:02:20,521
Did you want to get rid of me too?

1892
02:02:20,650 --> 02:02:21,775
Won't you listen to me ever girl?

1893
02:02:22,165 --> 02:02:23,290
Hey, tender damsel!

1894
02:02:24,981 --> 02:02:26,564
You make me laugh and make me cry.

1895
02:02:26,939 --> 02:02:28,439
Look,
how she is leaving swaying in style!

1896
02:02:28,731 --> 02:02:30,856
Look! A car has arrived at
brother Chandra's house!

1897
02:02:31,231 --> 02:02:32,522
His son-in-law must have come!

1898
02:02:33,189 --> 02:02:35,356
Oh, look!
Looks like son-in-law is here.

1899
02:02:35,564 --> 02:02:38,647
Let's welcome them and try
to unite the couple. Let's go.

1900
02:02:38,856 --> 02:02:41,897
- Let's do it!
- [all]: Let's unite both of them!

1901
02:02:42,189 --> 02:02:45,231
- Let's do it!
- [all]: Let's unite both of them!

1902
02:02:46,629 --> 02:02:47,671
Damini...

1903
02:02:47,696 --> 02:02:49,029
Please forgive us, dear.

1904
02:02:52,651 --> 02:02:53,984
Don't say like that, Mother-in-law.

1905
02:02:54,009 --> 02:02:55,134
You are elder to me.

1906
02:03:08,208 --> 02:03:11,916
You have brought a lot of changes
in our house without your knowledge.

1907
02:03:13,184 --> 02:03:18,392
Yadi who never cared for my words
ever, obeyed me for the first time.

1908
02:03:20,392 --> 02:03:24,100
Look, your father-in-laws who have
taken up to booze have changed.

1909
02:03:26,184 --> 02:03:28,184
You have seen an unchanging Yadi.

1910
02:03:28,911 --> 02:03:32,119
You should also see the love
of a changed Yadagiri, dear!

1911
02:03:36,809 --> 02:03:37,475
Come.

1912
02:03:37,517 --> 02:03:38,475
You go speak to her.

1913
02:03:41,642 --> 02:03:44,059
Damini, you shouldn't leave when
your mother-in-law is speaking to you.

1914
02:03:44,309 --> 02:03:46,767
Father-in-law, this is my problem.

1915
02:03:47,684 --> 02:03:48,684
I will take care of it.

1916
02:04:12,267 --> 02:04:14,142
I don't know where to start.

1917
02:04:16,975 --> 02:04:21,392
I feel like a wronged child
standing in front of a teacher.

1918
02:04:23,408 --> 02:04:24,533
Punish me if you want.

1919
02:04:25,059 --> 02:04:26,184
Give me an electric shock.

1920
02:04:27,059 --> 02:04:29,559
But don't say that you won't come home.

1921
02:04:30,559 --> 02:04:33,184
It seems you have saved
children in your village.

1922
02:04:34,017 --> 02:04:37,850
If you had done the same job in America,
I would have called you a superwoman.

1923
02:04:40,934 --> 02:04:42,684
Why don't you say something, Damini?

1924
02:04:44,017 --> 02:04:45,392
What should I say, Yadi?

1925
02:04:47,600 --> 02:04:49,225
You said it before
everyone in the house

1926
02:04:49,809 --> 02:04:51,850
that you could get
another girl in my place.

1927
02:04:53,985 --> 02:04:55,943
I lost my mother's
love when I was a child.

1928
02:04:56,892 --> 02:04:59,559
I thought I could get that
love when you came into my life.

1929
02:05:00,320 --> 02:05:01,362
But, what did you do?

1930
02:05:02,635 --> 02:05:03,677
You asked me to leave.

1931
02:05:04,600 --> 02:05:06,017
Anyway, why dig into the past?

1932
02:05:08,267 --> 02:05:10,684
Your parents have come from far away.

1933
02:05:12,350 --> 02:05:14,809
I can't hurt them by saying
that I won't come back.

1934
02:05:15,809 --> 02:05:19,059
Please say something and take them away.

1935
02:05:23,184 --> 02:05:24,642
Listen to what I have to say once.

1936
02:05:25,809 --> 02:05:30,100
When I thought have no property,
the lawyer told me about the will.

1937
02:05:31,142 --> 02:05:32,934
Tell me,
who doesn't have a desire for property?

1938
02:05:33,514 --> 02:05:38,764
I wanted get that property and save
my family and my grandfather's party.

1939
02:05:39,892 --> 02:05:44,100
That is why I came to this village
with the desire to marry someone.

1940
02:05:45,400 --> 02:05:52,365
But, I married you only
after liking you completely.

1941
02:06:08,844 --> 02:06:09,761
Damini...

1942
02:06:11,658 --> 02:06:15,200
I don't waste anything unnecessarily.
You too know that.

1943
02:06:16,017 --> 02:06:18,725
How did you think that
I would waste my love?

1944
02:06:42,392 --> 02:06:43,184
Damini.

1945
02:06:45,628 --> 02:06:47,211
That moon is also like you.

1946
02:06:48,934 --> 02:06:51,350
No one can either
touch it or grab it.

1947
02:06:55,475 --> 02:06:58,017
It gives light and courage
to those in the dark.

1948
02:06:58,677 --> 02:07:01,802
'That moon is also like you, dear.'

1949
02:07:02,017 --> 02:07:04,142
'No one can touch it or grab it.'

1950
02:07:06,619 --> 02:07:08,869
Where the moon is, everyone has light.

1951
02:07:09,044 --> 02:07:11,752
Everyone will know its value when it is
not there.

1952
02:07:12,017 --> 02:07:15,309
But, I knew its value when I lost it.

1953
02:07:17,731 --> 02:07:19,898
Would there be anyone
who doesn't like the moon?

1954
02:07:19,923 --> 02:07:22,590
Would there be people
who doesn't like the moon?

1955
02:07:43,517 --> 02:07:45,017
Yadhi.

1956
02:07:46,267 --> 02:07:47,434
Yadhi.

1957
02:07:49,892 --> 02:07:51,059
Yadhi, stop!

1958
02:08:21,517 --> 02:08:24,392
I fell in love with you when
I saw you for the first time.

1959
02:08:32,701 --> 02:08:34,617
Then, why did you leave me?

1960
02:08:35,184 --> 02:08:37,809
How is it my mistake?
You let me drift away from you.

1961
02:08:39,767 --> 02:08:40,684
Move.

1962
02:08:43,225 --> 02:08:44,725
Why am I not experiencing
an electric shock?

1963
02:08:46,302 --> 02:08:48,010
It's a problem if you get a shock.

1964
02:08:48,267 --> 02:08:50,392
How could there be a problem
if you don't experience a shock?

1965
02:08:52,517 --> 02:08:53,725
Oopsh!

1966
02:09:41,392 --> 02:09:42,934
Mother-in-law and others are here.

1967
02:09:43,726 --> 02:09:46,559
You are the
mother-in-law I like the most.

1968
02:09:47,434 --> 02:09:48,434
Damini.

1969
02:09:50,725 --> 02:09:52,475
- There's no shock!
- There's no shock!

1970
02:09:53,309 --> 02:09:54,350
There's no shock, Sister!

1971
02:09:54,809 --> 02:09:56,017
- There's no shock!
- There's none!

1972
02:09:56,517 --> 02:09:59,767
- There's no shock!
- Oldie, I will see your end.

1973
02:10:00,422 --> 02:10:02,603
Oldie? I'm just 20 years older than you.

1974
02:10:02,628 --> 02:10:04,045
Okay. I will touch you now.

1975
02:10:04,350 --> 02:10:05,142
There's no shock!

1976
02:10:05,167 --> 02:10:06,850
There's no shock!

1977
02:10:08,017 --> 02:10:10,767
I get gasbumps when I see this scene.

1978
02:10:11,100 --> 02:10:13,100
It's not "gasbumps," it's "goosebumps."

1979
02:10:13,434 --> 02:10:14,392
Mission passed.

1980
02:10:14,934 --> 02:10:16,517
Mission passed. Mission passed.

1981
02:10:17,475 --> 02:10:18,517
- Son-in-law!
- Good choice.

1982
02:10:18,725 --> 02:10:20,142
Good choice.

1983
02:10:23,809 --> 02:10:25,517
- Did she deliver?
- Aren't my parents here?

1984
02:10:25,951 --> 02:10:28,534
- Where are they?
- Did they go shopping for the baby?

1985
02:10:28,559 --> 02:10:29,184
They will come.

1986
02:10:29,847 --> 02:10:30,722
Greetings, Brother-in-law.

1987
02:10:34,059 --> 02:10:36,267
- I have a doubt, Father-in-law.
- Ask me, son.

1988
02:10:37,184 --> 02:10:38,892
I still don't understand.

1989
02:10:39,684 --> 02:10:41,350
How did your daughter
lose the electricity?

1990
02:10:42,350 --> 02:10:43,600
You still don't understand?

1991
02:10:43,934 --> 02:10:45,975
Damini sees her mother in you,
Son-in-law.

1992
02:10:49,475 --> 02:10:51,850
It is okay if your daughter
sees her mother in me.

1993
02:10:51,875 --> 02:10:53,375
But, don't see your wife in me.

1994
02:10:54,975 --> 02:10:56,017
Son-in-law.

1995
02:10:59,713 --> 02:11:00,796
It's a baby boy.

1996
02:11:04,979 --> 02:11:05,562
- Move!
- Move!

1997
02:11:06,332 --> 02:11:07,040
- Sir.
- Wait.

1998
02:11:07,211 --> 02:11:08,503
- Are you the father?
- Yes, I am.

1999
02:11:11,434 --> 02:11:13,392
I am doing such a
delivery for the first time.

2000
02:11:13,600 --> 02:11:15,892
When your son was born, all the
equipment inside was fried.

2001
02:11:16,142 --> 02:11:18,392
Add the equipment bill also
in the discharge summary.

